iner is hardened and will need machining to recover before new rings can be run in. Cermet is a composite, part-ceramic, part-metal material. It combines the best properties of a ceramic, i.e",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:bfe824ef46628149",`source`:"shipkg:fault:4de4eeb54341",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:bfe824ef46628149",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:d85a741773e8f8b9",`source_file`:"Frontiers_2021_marine_converter_oscillations.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/energy-research/articles/10.3389/fenrg.2020.529756/pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"sed in percentage terms. The limits are 0.5% for frequency and 5% for voltage. Well documented causes of such behavior include pulsating torque of generators’ prime movers and/or ﬂuctuating load, which combined with commonly used droop control method for load sharing, possibly leads to severe short and long-term frequency ﬂuctuations. However, little is known about the osci",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c081491485f5c7f9",`source`:"shipkg:observation:ec255ed61291",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c081491485f5c7f9",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:5350278460986ec7",`source_file`:"Azimuth_Thruster_CBM_Dataset.zip",`source_url`:"https://zenodo.org/records/20101612",`page`:"",`locator`:"table3_lti_by_fault_type_anonymised.csv:row9",`quote`:"System / engine-family case=CAT 3508B/C engine bearing reference; Fault or condition=Normal wear trend; Detection/event reference=Oil-led; ND (oil-led); Reference class=ND (oil-led); Recommended CBM action=Oil-led CBM; 500 h vibration / 125 h oil; Included in mechanical LTI summary=no",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c0837486a9c5f2c7",`source`:"shipkg:fault:c44e6c4545bf",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c0837486a9c5f2c7",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:a33dab8e3476ce99",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"20",`locator`:"PDF page 20",`quote`:"tarboard CPP back-up control mode was inadvertently selected, the master lost bridge control of that propeller. The starboard CPP continued to thrust at over half ahead throughout the vessel’s approach to the berth and up until its engine was stopped (about 2 hours after the contact). Starboard pitch back-up on/off control button Centre console lamps dimmer control buttons Figure 1: Part of brid",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c23595d7767e6e9a",`source`:"shipkg:condition:654fd1d6ce35",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"cooling",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c23595d7767e6e9a",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:2d4645410e75d447",`source_file`:"MAN_main_engine_auxiliary_efficiency.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/document-sync/efficiency-improvements-main-engine-auxiliary-systems-eng.pdf",`page`:"11",`locator`:"PDF page 11",`quote`:"ion and thereby increase cylinder wear. – Increased scavenge air temperature which will lead to increased fuel oil consumption. – A flow which is too low may cause local boiling on the water side inside the scavenge air cooler, which may lead to cavitation in the cooling water pipes. – The stated max. scavenge air temperature values given in the technical file may be exceeded, and the engine may thereby",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"cooling\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c35a5fd2a224fd5d",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:601948a19d34",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c35a5fd2a224fd5d",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:b2ab413559094e03",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"56",`locator`:"PDF page 56",`quote`:"workshops in Klaipeda. Despite this, seven of the intact 11 small ends removed from Finlandia Seaways’ engine were found to have notch damage on the internal surfaces of their small end eyes. Three of Botnia Seaways’ small ends had similar damage and three had evidence of localised heat damage. Although the technical investigations did not identify when the damage had been done, it was clearly apparent that it had be",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c51e4aa50f506ccd",`source`:"shipkg:fault:7dd3cdd4fe58",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c51e4aa50f506ccd",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:0f7534e3f93d98e3",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN033_bearing_currents.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-033_C-Shaft-Bearing-Currents.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"porting bearings, consequently any resulting current flow will pass across the rolling element of the bearings, and will initiate electrical erosion of the bearing materials, eventually reducing the low friction expectation of the bearing. It is possible for a single bearing alternator to suffer from shaft bearing currents, but here the current flow path at the drive end of the alternator’s shaft mus",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c5362d7e619c1835",`source`:"shipkg:condition:bdbca1b8295e",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c5362d7e619c1835",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:6522054ba5597880",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"Although the indicator for the turning gear, which was sited on the control panel, showed that the turning gear was in, this was poorly illuminated and was not seen by the engineer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage t",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c704966fd7702c2f",`source`:"shipkg:fault:562580f2bf5a",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"fuel_air",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c704966fd7702c2f",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:45f3ae7b802f6792",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"he accident as a basis for making recommendations to prevent similar accidents occurring in the future. 2.2 CAUSE OF THE FIRE The fire was initiated following the spray of hydraulic oil, from a ruptured pipework joint in the starboard CPP system, onto the hot exhaust uptakes of the starboard main engines. The flanged joint ruptured because the CPP system became over- pressurised as a result of t",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"fuel_air\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c7669cd06e67bc96",`source`:"shipkg:fault:7d56f05dfb4b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c7669cd06e67bc96",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:f4ea99f2d07cb7c1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"en Mary 2 (QM2) was approaching Barcelona, an explosion occurred in the vessel’s aft main switchboard room. Within a few seconds, all four propulsion motors shut down, and the vessel blacked out shortly afterwards. Fortunately, the vessel was clear of navigational hazards and drifted in open sea. The emergency generator started automatically and provided essential supplies to the vessel, and i",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c7ef3bb2ae471c8b",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:89c72d5dc590",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"cooling",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c7ef3bb2ae471c8b",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:e7c09d475a3dc5ea",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"59",`locator`:"PDF page 59",`quote`:"on deck sorting a previous catch. The skipper returned to the wheelhouse to investigate the noises and found that the engine room bilge high level alarm was illuminated and sounding. The skipper instructed the engineer to go to the engine room and investigate. The engineer observed that water was almost level with the top of the main engine and was rising quickly. He started the bilge pump but could not reac",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"cooling\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c820bdbff44ea7ff",`source`:"shipkg:cause:0b368a5a5869",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c820bdbff44ea7ff",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:a4a51bca0c30f80d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"f the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the metal-to-metal contact between surfaces of the connecting rods and their bearing caps. This would have caused fretting wear between the mating faces, which would have led to loosening and rapid failure of the end cap securing bolts. [2.3.2] 5. Four of",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cab1dcb305214f67",`source`:"shipkg:action:fa948d692647",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cab1dcb305214f67",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7331136605690ccd",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"sing water level, which was now above the bottom plates. Worried about potential damage to machinery, he left the bilge system to stop the generator and main engine, and sent the motorman to the bridge to tell the master that the engine room was flooding. With the water level continuing to rise, the chief engineer evacuated the engine room, leaving open the watertight door between the engine",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cac6825d9c475b0f",`source`:"shipkg:check:64ccf3c3f401",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cac6825d9c475b0f",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:aee93ed7c1866eb1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"id not fully understand the vessel’s propulsion control system and had not routinely tested their back-up and emergency controls. Regular testing of back-up and emergency control systems, and the conduct of machinery breakdown drills, provide the most effective method of ensuring the crew fully understand their ship’s systems and are best prepared to respond in an emergency. Figure 3: Damage to linkspan, mooring",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cb3ddfe52bf5880e",`source`:"shipkg:fault:423cd9a63be0",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cb3ddfe52bf5880e",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:390711bc162bb6ce",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"r Susan suffered a catastrophic failure of a diesel generator engine while conducting sea trials in the Firth of Forth, Scotland. The failure resulted in an engine room fire and a complete power blackout. The crew responded promptly, extinguished the fire and mustered safely. The vessel lost propulsion and began drifting eastwards. Attempts to deploy anchors were unsuccessful because the anchor winches required electrical power t",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cb4ff396f327807b",`source`:"shipkg:condition:725f6ac0521d",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cb4ff396f327807b",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:de200230bb22400e",`source_file`:"Frontiers_2021_marine_converter_oscillations.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/energy-research/articles/10.3389/fenrg.2020.529756/pdf",`page`:"6",`locator`:"PDF page 6",`quote`:"rd 45.1, 2017). Since the majority of loads had linear characteristic and did not vary, such a behavior is to be associated with power converter control under the condition of signi ﬁcantly varying frequency at the shaft generator terminal. Moreover, the level of all parameters oscillation was the highest of all analyzed ships. Research Onboard of Research-Training Ship The case study for the res",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cc1de282bd938b10",`source`:"shipkg:component:784cd78efb12",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cc1de282bd938b10",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:b10e854dd960072c",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"ate without any problems and the vessel undertook several voyages. However, after the engine failure, the duplex filter was found without a filter cartridge in the on-line filter chamber, and the engine lubricating oil system was contaminated. The contamination caused main bearing seizure, the rotation of bearing shells and the blockage of oil ways, and subsequent oil starvation and",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cc9862f12545a7bf",`source`:"shipkg:fault:f078b5a27275",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cc9862f12545a7bf",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4812bf9684b2b7ad",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"14 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 5 The Lessons 1. Ergonomically, the layout of the bridge console was not well designed. The close proximity of the safety-critical propulsion control buttons and the similar looking everyday use dimmer buttons, increased the likelihood of the type of human error seen in this case. There is always a risk that watchkeepers and equipment operators will inadvertently press the wrong butto",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cd682045af58d32f",`source`:"shipkg:equipment:385291025daa",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"fuel_air",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cd682045af58d32f",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:861eb8fbe47cd585",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"f pressurised fuel. The fuel sprayed onto the exposed exhaust manifold that was operating at a temperature exceeding 220°C when a screw in a two-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by anti-splashing tape or shielding and fuel was able to escape forcefully. [2.3.2] 3. Th",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"fuel_air\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cdb32d5b36633328",`source`:"shipkg:component:6f0aead2b5a6",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cdb32d5b36633328",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4f930aa49cf38734",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"ch went according to plan until the ferry was about 1½ ships’ length from its final berthing position, when her three main engine clutches disengaged almost simultaneously. No Air, No Clutch, No CPP , No Brakes Damage to lubrication oil pipe and bottom end bearing Bottom end bearing Failed lubricant oil pipe end fitting",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cdc8c2f3e343d47a",`source`:"shipkg:cause:c5d7e29b6c94",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"cooling",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cdc8c2f3e343d47a",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:9282652d0f980004",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2016_623_cooling_water.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-623.pdf",`page`:"3",`locator`:"PDF page 3",`quote`:"ontent ≤50 mg/l ≤50 mg/l 2) Fig. 3: Rust and limescale blocks the cooling water bores (valve seat removed from cylinder head) The quality of the freshwater must be checked using the MAN Diesel & Turbo water testing kit or a similar test kit pro - vided by the manufacturer. The requirements to freshwater quality are stated in Table 1. Treatment and periodical checks of the cooling water W hen distil",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"cooling\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cecbd6c43807af5b",`source`:"shipkg:fault:8027eb707475",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cecbd6c43807af5b",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:157ede421b19ee3a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"neer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage to the shaft and gearing (Figure 1) and to the turning gear casing (Figure 2) disabled the ship for a month and cost a six-figure sum to repair. To Turn or Not to Turn?",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cf401d690ced2897",`source`:"shipkg:condition:7647f12090ef",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cf401d690ced2897",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4812bf9684b2b7ad",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"14 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 5 The Lessons 1. Ergonomically, the layout of the bridge console was not well designed. The close proximity of the safety-critical propulsion control buttons and the similar looking everyday use dimmer buttons, increased the likelihood of the type of human error seen in this case. There is always a risk that watchkeepers and equipment operators will inadvertently press the wrong butto",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cf940a5dc7aaa340",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:ccae4eb65c57",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cf940a5dc7aaa340",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:5124f3b43ff47b3a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"70",`locator`:"PDF page 70",`quote`:"ymington River. The engine was running at full speed (1800rpm) and was driving the forward VSP unit in parallel with ME1 when its ECU detected a loss of lubricating oil pressure and initiated an engine shutdown. 63 seconds later, the engine’s number four connecting rod and piston assembly was thrown out of the crankcase into the engine room. The engine had accumulated 2241 running hours and had been installed 11 months earlier as a new",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d077a433da85db69",`source`:"shipkg:equipment:38482b664e19",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d077a433da85db69",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:f4e14e047a77ffb2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"n by the engineer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage to the shaft and gearing (Figure 1) and to the turning gear casing (Figure 2) disabled the ship for a month and cost a six-figure sum to repair. To Turn",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d0b9c5868e5c79de",`source`:"shipkg:action:32b0fb5f9f2b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"fuel_air",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d0b9c5868e5c79de",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:e9d71048b791d31a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"as a result of it being insufficiently tightened by shore staff during a recent dry dock. • A section of the adjacent generator’s exhaust piping had been left unlagged following its overhaul during the recent dry dock (Figure 2b). This was hidden from view by the exhaust casing. • Fine oil spray ignited when it came into contact with the hot exhaust casing. Figure 1: Location of the generator w",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"fuel_air\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d247ffbc56785058",`source`:"shipkg:equipment:00688defba1b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"fuel_air",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d247ffbc56785058",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:e9d71048b791d31a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"as a result of it being insufficiently tightened by shore staff during a recent dry dock. • A section of the adjacent generator’s exhaust piping had been left unlagged following its overhaul during the recent dry dock (Figure 2b). This was hidden from view by the exhaust casing. • Fine oil spray ignited when it came into contact with the hot exhaust casing. Figure 1: Location of the generator w",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"fuel_air\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d3f31e2b9e6900a7",`source`:"shipkg:sensor:8ab013653446",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"cooling",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d3f31e2b9e6900a7",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:e404f4ecf4526f44",`source_file`:"Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip",`source_url`:"https://zenodo.org/records/19857425",`page`:"",`locator`:"variable_dictionary.csv:Engine Cooling water flow",`quote`:"full_name=Engine Cooling water flow; symbol=Qw_eng; unit=m3/h; dtype=number; in_reference=TRUE; in_scenario_files=TRUE; category=flow / fuel / air",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"cooling\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d6b979f742fbd27b",`source`:"shipkg:action:6e0e5173ee8f",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d6b979f742fbd27b",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1ed28429bcfc3816",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"tion of this button bypassed the feedback control system, giving direct control of pitch to the pitch control lever. However, the master was not familiar with its use, and therefore lost the opportunity to bring the vessel back under control before it struck the quay. It was also revealed during the investigation that the system parameters for astern pitch control had been incorrectly set duri",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d712e0bcd64b4b1f",`source`:"shipkg:action:984af3c3d6c8",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d712e0bcd64b4b1f",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1b6ee0d38c733128",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"6",`locator`:"PDF page 6",`quote`:"edules are only applicable for these parts. Non-Caterpillar parts used in the engine tent to have a shorter service life. [sic] • Check the use of non-Caterpillar bearings in the other engines on the vessel. If so, plan a early change of the main and connecting rod bearings. [sic] Parts approval process The approval process for a ship’s engine parts involved several steps to ensure compliance with safety and performanc",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d71de3b270d04fa6",`source`:"shipkg:condition:290bfe38530e",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d71de3b270d04fa6",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:2d8d8f05ec0d8390",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"tective covers over safety- critical buttons, switches and knobs. 2. The master was confident that he had control of his CPPs and did not look at the pitch indicators located on the control consoles. Had he done so he would have realised the starboard CPP was not responding to his orders. 3. The ship’s engineers recognised that something was untoward well before the master had committed to his",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d7b369af0d270178",`source`:"shipkg:fault:e97eee073fc6",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d7b369af0d270178",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:755b4102fd859a55",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"y’s pitching caused the propellers to come out of the water. This caused a sudden reduction in torque on the propulsion motor and led to a very rapid increase in the motors’ rpm. The engine alarm and monitoring system recorded that, immediately before their shutdown, the rpm of each pod’s propulsion motor very rapidly increased and exceeded the preset overspeed limitation. The pod’s PCS therefore automat",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d88125ee68c967a9",`source`:"shipkg:fault:9b76a4f68834",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d88125ee68c967a9",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:3ca79df2a0332a1a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"igh levels of vibration, and contaminated lubricating oil might all have contributed to the event failure. [2.3.1] 3. Wight Sky’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d882b3b91b7cc765",`source`:"shipkg:sensor:5c7b83264f58",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d882b3b91b7cc765",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:942baa3ea69a9e36",`source_file`:"Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip",`source_url`:"https://zenodo.org/records/19857425",`page`:"",`locator`:"variable_dictionary.csv:LO Temp. Engine Out",`quote`:"full_name=LO Temp. Engine Out; symbol=T11; unit=°C; dtype=number; in_reference=TRUE; in_scenario_files=TRUE; category=temperature",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d960ed1837a80970",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:89c72d5dc590",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d960ed1837a80970",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:e7c09d475a3dc5ea",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"59",`locator`:"PDF page 59",`quote`:"on deck sorting a previous catch. The skipper returned to the wheelhouse to investigate the noises and found that the engine room bilge high level alarm was illuminated and sounding. The skipper instructed the engineer to go to the engine room and investigate. The engineer observed that water was almost level with the top of the main engine and was rising quickly. He started the bilge pump but could not reac",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d99cd37d10a0b2ca",`source`:"shipkg:fault:0ad9453d012b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"cooling",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d99cd37d10a0b2ca",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:fbe07737c9447c24",`source_file`:"MAN_main_engine_auxiliary_efficiency.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/document-sync/efficiency-improvements-main-engine-auxiliary-systems-eng.pdf",`page`:"11",`locator`:"PDF page 11",`quote`:"d fuel oil consumption. – A flow which is too low may cause local boiling on the water side inside the scavenge air cooler, which may lead to cavitation in the cooling water pipes. – The stated max. scavenge air temperature values given in the technical file may be exceeded, and the engine may thereby not fulfil the Tier II NO X requirements. On this basis, a system has to be established that maintains a c",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"cooling\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:dbe9a176be30a55b",`source`:"shipkg:fault:8027eb707475",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:dbe9a176be30a55b",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:157ede421b19ee3a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"neer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage to the shaft and gearing (Figure 1) and to the turning gear casing (Figure 2) disabled the ship for a month and cost a six-figure sum to repair. To Turn or Not to Turn?",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:dca7b47fea947659",`source`:"shipkg:action:984af3c3d6c8",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:dca7b47fea947659",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1b6ee0d38c733128",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"6",`locator`:"PDF page 6",`quote`:"edules are only applicable for these parts. Non-Caterpillar parts used in the engine tent to have a shorter service life. [sic] • Check the use of non-Caterpillar bearings in the other engines on the vessel. If so, plan a early change of the main and connecting rod bearings. [sic] Parts approval process The approval process for a ship’s engine parts involved several steps to ensure compliance with safety and performanc",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:de02a35079302b7d",`source`:"shipkg:fault:aba0717d72a0",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:de02a35079302b7d",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:09940c64e5709cec",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"n-line filter chamber, and the engine lubricating oil system was contaminated. The contamination caused main bearing seizure, the rotation of bearing shells and the blockage of oil ways, and subsequent oil starvation and overheating to other bearings and to the pistons. The engine daily logs referred to oil filter cartridge changes only prior to the repair to the oil pumps. They also showed that the pressure rea",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:dfd7be3e6c333195",`source`:"shipkg:equipment:024350fd8dee",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:dfd7be3e6c333195",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:af6ff177f229c6a2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e suppression spray heads were activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectric fluid vapour spr",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e0e070bfbe91c603",`source`:"shipkg:component:3295e52dd075",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e0e070bfbe91c603",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:dc67d8904baddd49",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"led, but fortunately the damage was above the waterline (Figure 1). The subsequent investigation identified that the vessel had a history of sluggish astern response. However, the crew had accepted this as a ‘characteristic’ of the vessel and usually compensated for it by demanding astern movements well in advance. The CPP control panel on the bridge had a back-up control button (Figure 2) fo",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e12b266b69ca749e",`source`:"shipkg:fault:f6eb639558ed",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e12b266b69ca749e",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1e17c52e491ed79c",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN235_torsional_analysis.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-235_A-Generating-Set-Assembly-Torsional-Vibration-Analysis.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"ng the extremely rapid pressure pulse of a burning air fuel mixture above the piston. The engine produces power in pulses and the pulses can excite very significant resonant responses. The pulsing of the power produced by the combustion process translates to angular vibrations in the crank shaft of the engine. The magnitude of the vibration depends on the number of cylinders in the engine. The movement of an i",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e14f80df341c3096",`source`:"shipkg:equipment:5d25f4bda048",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e14f80df341c3096",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:9c5f7101c8442b54",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"15",`locator`:"PDF page 15",`quote`:"essel was able to berth safely alongside, assisted by harbour tugs. Subsequent investigation identified that No2 compressor had a damaged discharge valve. Neither compressor had been able to keep up with demand.",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e1b95b1cc02cad1e",`source`:"shipkg:action:4578c5b2c727",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"fuel_air",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e1b95b1cc02cad1e",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1ba466d574203869",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"31",`locator`:"PDF page 31",`quote`:"s for the purpose of regular hot spot monitoring and detection in machinery spaces. ● Modified the external fuel piping on ME3 to incorporate four-screw flanges. ● Repaired or replaced the shielding and lagging around the external fuel systems and hot surfaces and fitted anti-splashing tape to all joints on the low-pressure fuel systems on all of Stena Europe’s operational engines. ● On",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"fuel_air\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e28e806c06e01ed8",`source`:"shipkg:component:d16e663b1271",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e28e806c06e01ed8",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:470e8782d7a79377",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"t in the starboard CPP system, onto the hot exhaust uptakes of the starboard main engines. The flanged joint ruptured because the CPP system became over- pressurised as a result of the back pressure valve (PSV3) becoming jammed in the closed position. The reason for the temporary increase in the starboard main engine load to 100% and corresponding increase in turbocharger rpm has not been det",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e3786b9f143b8da2",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:fa4424a6b543",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e3786b9f143b8da2",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:b0c29f0e315a7acd",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"19",`locator`:"PDF page 19",`quote`:"continued towards the port. However, a few minutes later the engineers in the engine control room noticed that the starboard CPP back-up control system indicator lamp was illuminated on their console. Having not seen this before, they discussed its significance before deciding to take no immediate action. As the vessel entered the port the master reduced speed by decreasing the pitch settings on the port and",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e397399f38296bd2",`source`:"shipkg:action:d556abb4fcfa",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e397399f38296bd2",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:dee08b2e20581c60",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"23",`locator`:"PDF page 23",`quote`:"wrong. 3. An oil mist detector gives advance warning of an impending major failure. When a detector alarm occurs, the thought of stopping and inspecting the engine as soon as possible should be uppermost in an engineer’s mind. The consequences of ignoring it are clear, and expensive.",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e4a67580c64a5cf6",`source`:"shipkg:condition:3516d66bca42",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e4a67580c64a5cf6",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:9eb024fc4137b406",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN033_bearing_currents.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-033_C-Shaft-Bearing-Currents.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"aft within a rotating electrical machine - motor or alternator – to come under the influence of magnetic fields which result in a voltage (electrical pressure) generated along the axial length of the shaft. This ‘shaft voltage’ will then force current to flow from one end of the shaft, along a path which is radially out of the shaft through an end bracket continue along the alternators stator fra",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e56d6bd22a576411",`source`:"shipkg:sensor:482eb47f8513",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e56d6bd22a576411",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:c9d838c8d843eeee",`source_file`:"Marine_Engine_Fault_Data_v1.zip",`source_url`:"https://zenodo.org/records/19857425",`page`:"",`locator`:"variable_dictionary.csv:Shaft Power",`quote`:"full_name=Shaft Power; symbol=Ws; unit=kW; dtype=number; in_reference=TRUE; in_scenario_files=TRUE; category=other",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e5e03964a7c9d8df",`source`:"shipkg:component:6432d2482f06",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e5e03964a7c9d8df",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:157ede421b19ee3a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"neer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage to the shaft and gearing (Figure 1) and to the turning gear casing (Figure 2) disabled the ship for a month and cost a six-figure sum to repair. To Turn or Not to Turn?",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e65648eeb6f4a928",`source`:"shipkg:condition:2ee58a9a8fad",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e65648eeb6f4a928",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:5e9ac17b88449c65",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"53",`locator`:"PDF page 53",`quote`:"s: ● Created an additional seakeeping and manoeuvring decision support poster and software tool for the Spirit Class vessels that includes propeller exposure in wave heights up to 10.5m.",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e660c93bbdb82aca",`source`:"shipkg:condition:4e433b14487c",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e660c93bbdb82aca",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:0bd224f4476f3548",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN076_alternator_bearings.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/2024-04/AGN076_C.pdf",`page`:"4",`locator`:"PDF page 4",`quote`:"e expected, but the bearings might well be failing for different reasons. For example; where a ball bearing might fail because of axial vibration, causing a fretting action in the housing, the cylindrical roller bearing might fail because of lack of grease or misalignment damage. The anti-friction ball bearings used on STAMFORD alternators are not insulated bearings. The design of STAMFORD alternato",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e6fc20b5afd7b37d",`source`:"shipkg:fault:7d56f05dfb4b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e6fc20b5afd7b37d",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:f4ea99f2d07cb7c1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"en Mary 2 (QM2) was approaching Barcelona, an explosion occurred in the vessel’s aft main switchboard room. Within a few seconds, all four propulsion motors shut down, and the vessel blacked out shortly afterwards. Fortunately, the vessel was clear of navigational hazards and drifted in open sea. The emergency generator started automatically and provided essential supplies to the vessel, and i",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e8cd2ef344b47d4d",`source`:"shipkg:check:de8a5b9844ad",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e8cd2ef344b47d4d",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:d2bfff6df47b53cc",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"18",`locator`:"PDF page 18",`quote`:"2013 The Lessons 1. The turning gear interlock had not been included within the planned maintenance system on board and there was no record of it having been tested. 2. Control console illumination panels are vital to the safe operation of machinery and should therefore be tested regularly. If problems with visual indication or warning lamps cannot be rectified immediately, they must be repo",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e9759bdb899dbec9",`source`:"shipkg:observation:5d48f4f61abd",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e9759bdb899dbec9",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:b935264465ef205c",`source_file`:"Azimuth_Thruster_CBM_Dataset.zip",`source_url`:"https://zenodo.org/records/20101612",`page`:"",`locator`:"table3_lti_by_fault_type_anonymised.csv:row7",`quote`:"System / engine-family case=CAT 3516C intermediate bearing EB 4; Fault or condition=Unconfirmed bearing-related warning; Detection/event reference=Vibration alert Month -2.0; maintenance event; Reference class=LTI_maintenance; LTI / warning (mo)=2.0; Warning (h)=300.0; Recommended CBM action=Vibration-only CBM; 125 h vibration interval; Included in mechanical LTI summary=yes",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e9b0f37033e21813",`source`:"shipkg:component:960fe73dbb4b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e9b0f37033e21813",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:8e948de9b710ce4f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"ond compressor (No2) and reported his actions to the senior engineer in the ECR. Immediate investigation identified that the main lubricating oil discharge pipe assembly in No1 compressor had detached, and that the bottom end bearing had overheated and failed (see figure). No1 compressor was isolated but the engineers soon noticed that the air pressure in the main air receiver was dropping. Short",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:ea027a84acae7cff",`source`:"shipkg:equipment:6cc9aa419de7",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:ea027a84acae7cff",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:45cb3bc7993a557f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"y’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the metal-to-metal contact between surfaces of the connecting rods and their bearing caps. This would have caused fr",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:eaa95f7f563acf08",`source`:"shipkg:check:64ccf3c3f401",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:eaa95f7f563acf08",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:aee93ed7c1866eb1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"id not fully understand the vessel’s propulsion control system and had not routinely tested their back-up and emergency controls. Regular testing of back-up and emergency control systems, and the conduct of machinery breakdown drills, provide the most effective method of ensuring the crew fully understand their ship’s systems and are best prepared to respond in an emergency. Figure 3: Damage to linkspan, mooring",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:eb3433ff68f18d3e",`source`:"shipkg:condition:bdbca1b8295e",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:eb3433ff68f18d3e",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:6522054ba5597880",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"Although the indicator for the turning gear, which was sited on the control panel, showed that the turning gear was in, this was poorly illuminated and was not seen by the engineer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage t",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f0265b7c7608e004",`source`:"shipkg:condition:8012db626950",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"fuel_air",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f0265b7c7608e004",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:3b167c1e7ff25a89",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by anti-splashing tape or shielding and fuel was able to escape forcefully. [2.3.2] 3. The engine manufacturer’s recommended fuel system modification had been fitted to the external fuel system of just one of Stena Europe’s four main engines. The opportunity to fit",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"fuel_air\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f16e7ed6126a5ae7",`source`:"shipkg:fault:5f59e6b3ca42",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f16e7ed6126a5ae7",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:9094aa614ec060db",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"ntrolled environment and transferring it complete into the engine room would have reduced the likelihood of debris ingress. • The engine was not fitted with a wear detector, so there was no means of receiving a warning before the engine failed. • The essential services switchboard aft circuit breaker had been left in manual mode, resulting in the loss of power to critical equipment, including the fixed fire-fighting system. ACTION TAKEN Wightli",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f1c220f7c37e066a",`source`:"shipkg:fault:675217222811",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f1c220f7c37e066a",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:2cdda8701b9f350e",`source_file`:"MAIB_2017_20_Hebrides_CPP_coupling.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/59b7ab1c40f0b61231e71a54/MAIBInvReport20_2017.pdf",`page`:"30",`locator`:"PDF page 30",`quote`:"CONTROL FAILURE MECHANISM It is evident from the inspection carried out by Hebrides’s engineers shortly after the accident, that control of the ferry’s port CPP was lost due to a mechanical failure within the linear servomotor actuator sited on the port gearbox (Figure 6). The setscrew used to secure one half of the jaw coupling to the stepper motor ‘D’ shaped shaft had backed off from the shaft’",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f2ca87dce41f253c",`source`:"shipkg:check:e53578d74732",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"cooling",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f2ca87dce41f253c",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:9282652d0f980004",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2016_623_cooling_water.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-623.pdf",`page`:"3",`locator`:"PDF page 3",`quote`:"ontent ≤50 mg/l ≤50 mg/l 2) Fig. 3: Rust and limescale blocks the cooling water bores (valve seat removed from cylinder head) The quality of the freshwater must be checked using the MAN Diesel & Turbo water testing kit or a similar test kit pro - vided by the manufacturer. The requirements to freshwater quality are stated in Table 1. Treatment and periodical checks of the cooling water W hen distil",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"cooling\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f369442f930591a9",`source`:"shipkg:fault:562580f2bf5a",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f369442f930591a9",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:45f3ae7b802f6792",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"he accident as a basis for making recommendations to prevent similar accidents occurring in the future. 2.2 CAUSE OF THE FIRE The fire was initiated following the spray of hydraulic oil, from a ruptured pipework joint in the starboard CPP system, onto the hot exhaust uptakes of the starboard main engines. The flanged joint ruptured because the CPP system became over- pressurised as a result of t",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f44931e0d75b1336",`source`:"shipkg:fault:a20cef558a0a",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f44931e0d75b1336",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:45cb3bc7993a557f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"y’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the metal-to-metal contact between surfaces of the connecting rods and their bearing caps. This would have caused fr",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f4672d81488003a7",`source`:"shipkg:equipment:361590fc68c0",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"cooling",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f4672d81488003a7",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:2180f44fb45d636d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"ssel. Are you prepared for a flooding emergency? 3. Examination of the isolating valve following the accident identified that the valve actuator had been defective, giving an impression that the valve was fully closed when it was not. Although there was a visual indicator located on the side of the actuator, this was not checked to confirm that the valve was closed prior to removal of the f",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"cooling\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f4c38529fcb51c1f",`source`:"shipkg:fault:74505aa1776a",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f4c38529fcb51c1f",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:44f19b4f5b32f488",`source_file`:"Azimuth_Thruster_CBM_Dataset.zip",`source_url`:"https://zenodo.org/records/20101612",`page`:"",`locator`:"table3_lti_by_fault_type_anonymised.csv:row4",`quote`:"System / engine-family case=CAT 3516C coupling EB 1; Fault or condition=Coupling resonance; Detection/event reference=Vibration alert Month -2.0; maintenance event; Reference class=LTI_maintenance; LTI / warning (mo)=2.0; Warning (h)=300.0; Recommended CBM action=Vibration-led CBM; 125 h vibration / 500 h oil; Included in mechanical LTI summary=yes",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f5466def9fbd982a",`source`:"shipkg:condition:8012db626950",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f5466def9fbd982a",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:3b167c1e7ff25a89",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by anti-splashing tape or shielding and fuel was able to escape forcefully. [2.3.2] 3. The engine manufacturer’s recommended fuel system modification had been fitted to the external fuel system of just one of Stena Europe’s four main engines. The opportunity to fit",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f5554490157ed0c6",`source`:"shipkg:fault:323fee48e778",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f5554490157ed0c6",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:8b5ccc7bfc9235d4",`source_file`:"TSRF_main.zip",`source_url`:"https://github.com/TS-RF/TSRF",`page`:"",`locator`:"data/Ring-adhesion.csv",`quote`:"Ring-adhesion.csv",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:BELONGS_TO_SYSTEM {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_23 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:f5679f933af5dd6a",`source`:"shipkg:component:e0a03cf176fe",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"fuel_air",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f5679f933af5dd6a",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:861eb8fbe47cd585",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"f pressurised fuel. The fuel sprayed onto the exposed exhaust manifold that was operating at a temperature exceeding 220°C when a screw in a two-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by anti-splashing tape or shielding and fuel was able to escape forcefully. [2.3.2] 3. Th",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"fuel_air\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f609ab43aaccb8c6",`source`:"shipkg:action:84a87c035a24",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f609ab43aaccb8c6",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:d1a2571c248baad4",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"e was safely released from the suction side of the pump by using the bleed nut on the suction strainer. • Ensuring that the inlet flange was split in a controlled manner with a number of loosened bolts still in situ to enable them to be re-tightened in the event of the isolating valve not holding. 2. The crew’s response to the flooding was ineffective because they were not prepared for the emerge",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f95f6bbe851a6ae8",`source`:"shipkg:condition:133adfa97595",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"cooling",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f95f6bbe851a6ae8",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:6d6d03a1efd0d418",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"60",`locator`:"PDF page 60",`quote`:"ated as designed, with no one present in the wheelhouse to either see or hear it, it was not detected in time to save the vessel. Never leave the wheelhouse unmanned when underway; doing so is in contravention of the COLREGs and puts you and your vessel at risk. 2. The crew were instructed to enter the accommodation to collect lifejackets in preparation for abandoning the vessel, but instead took personal",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"cooling\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:fad2b7fdbf57beee",`source`:"shipkg:condition:db2e89c50479",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"fuel_air",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:fad2b7fdbf57beee",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:3bea0430b472030b",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"64",`locator`:"PDF page 64",`quote`:"current imbalance transformer were tested during manufacture, subsequent tests of the system were by secondary current injection, bypassing the windings. As the IAS did not specifically register which rank of the HF had developed an imbalance current, it was not possible to confirm if the current imbalance transformers on rank 1 1.3 had ever worked in service. It is concerning th",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"fuel_air\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:fdfcfa912161d0f0",`source`:"shipkg:equipment:61cd855f5970",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"transmission",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:fdfcfa912161d0f0",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:0b7a42308cc8b6cc",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"D OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silica sand and other abrasive particles embe",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"transmission\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:fe7ae1fd68f1211c",`source`:"shipkg:fault:41a15c8ffad7",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"cooling",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:fe7ae1fd68f1211c",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4cdcbf4e0a149c7e",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2016_623_cooling_water.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-623.pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"t in thermal overload of the components to be cooled by the engine cooling water. A thermal overload may, however, also result in cracks and leakages as seen in the exhaust valve seat ring. Insufficient cooling water flow has widespread consequenc - es, in many cases this will influence the combustion process as well and therefore the overall performance and safety of Fig. 1:",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"cooling\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:ff2bc2e691b752a6",`source`:"shipkg:fault:c8fa85d36573",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"electrical",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:ff2bc2e691b752a6",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:f17ab4bbdcec2bfc",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e suppression spray heads were activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectri",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"electrical\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:ff8cce45e75fb388",`source`:"shipkg:component:0dcadce61c82",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"fuel_air",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:ff8cce45e75fb388",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:9c5f7101c8442b54",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"15",`locator`:"PDF page 15",`quote`:"essel was able to berth safely alongside, assisted by harbour tugs. Subsequent investigation identified that No2 compressor had a damaged discharge valve. Neither compressor had been able to keep up with demand.",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"fuel_air\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:ffd0b2d7d280b726",`source`:"shipkg:condition:6fa538170906",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`classification_rule`:"lubrication",`name`:"归属系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:ffd0b2d7d280b726",`case_id`:"",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1b6ee0d38c733128",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"6",`locator`:"PDF page 6",`quote`:"edules are only applicable for these parts. Non-Caterpillar parts used in the engine tent to have a shorter service life. [sic] • Check the use of non-Caterpillar bearings in the other engines on the vessel. If so, plan a early change of the main and connecting rod bearings. [sic] Parts approval process The approval process for a ship’s engine parts involved several steps to ensure compliance with safety and performanc",`props_json`:"{\"classification_rule\": \"lubrication\", \"name\": \"归属系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"BELONGS_TO_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:BELONGS_TO_SYSTEM {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_24 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:00bdaedd5815def3",`source`:"shipkg:case:adf367a46f33",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:00bdaedd5815def3",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me2_2018",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4846a9af2b7e6456",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"S 3.1 SAFETY ISSUES DIRECTLY CONTRIBUTING TO THE ACCIDENTS THAT HAVE BEEN ADDRESSED OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silic",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:0161f5694aa52822",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:bff048b48ff1",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:0161f5694aa52822",`case_id`:"knowledge:generator_bearing_wear",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:65e2c4b3facd8c2b",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN076_alternator_bearings.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/2024-04/AGN076_C.pdf",`page`:"4",`locator`:"PDF page 4",`quote`:"t fail because of axial vibration, causing a fretting action in the housing, the cylindrical roller bearing might fail because of lack of grease or misalignment damage. The anti-friction ball bearings used on STAMFORD alternators are not insulated bearings. The design of STAMFORD alternators is such that the shaft does not come under the influence of magnetic fields that result in excessive vol",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:0711483a996071c6",`source`:"shipkg:case:213f8edb92c2",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:0711483a996071c6",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:af6ff177f229c6a2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e suppression spray heads were activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectric fluid vapour spr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:08f490051756c0e1",`source`:"shipkg:case:d6e9f8f8ade2",`target`:"shipkg:system:5d1dca19fd66",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:08f490051756c0e1",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:eb8d9ba0db21fede",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"9",`locator`:"PDF page 9",`quote`:"ent and Incident Investigation Division and the engine manufacturer, MAN Diesel and Turbo SE. The investigation identified that a fracture of the connecting rod small end had led to the sudden failure of the main engine. The investigation also found that the method used to replace the connecting rod small end piston pin bearing bushes by the vessel manager’s maintenance support contractor had intr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:137bedc55f074afb",`source`:"shipkg:case:ad49b658b30b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:137bedc55f074afb",`case_id`:"sd2016_14_sea_valve",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:b7715f5c139d9453",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"33 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 14 Fail to Plan, Plan to Fail Narrative On a fine day, a general cargo vessel was on passage with a cargo of limestone. The master was on watch on the bridge. In the engine room, the chief engineer, motorman and a seaman were undertaking maintenance on one of the two main ballast pumps; the chief engineer",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:14dc19c5ae0a6cd0",`source`:"shipkg:case:63aa8b018e0d",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:14dc19c5ae0a6cd0",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:57049bc52d7488e2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"7",`locator`:"PDF page 7",`quote`:"mage to the port main engine room and rendered one of its four main engines inoperative for several weeks. The fire was caused by fuel leaking under pressure from the fuel system of main engine number 3 and igniting on an exposed hot surface. No one was injured and there was no pollution. The investigation found that the fuel had ignited on part of the engine’s exhaust system that had",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:17e7a6ef674e91d1",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:8a35cec932af",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:17e7a6ef674e91d1",`case_id`:"knowledge:damper_failure",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:71b1d838f3e59389",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2017_654_torsional_damper.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2017-654.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"oil - r educed lube oil supply - c ontaminated lube oil leading to carbon built up internal the damper b y the centrifugal forces will reduce the service life of the torsional vibration damper and may lead to failure before reaching the mentioned operation limits. Indications of a failing torsional vibration damper could be abnormal noise from the torsional vibration damper or any chan",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:1900f0977ec59f80",`source`:"shipkg:case:187dc871fbd5",`target`:"shipkg:system:dacba8b43ef4",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:1900f0977ec59f80",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:c3429f0fc22579e1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"e vessel’s heading. Given the weather conditions at the time, it is almost certain that Spirit of Discovery’s pitching caused the propellers to come out of the water. This caused a sudden reduction in torque on the propulsion motor and led to a very rapid increase in the motors’ rpm. The engine alarm and monitoring system recorded that, immediately before their shutdown, the rpm of each pod’s",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:1bbb91e1fb7034b8",`source`:"shipkg:case:ffc594a9fab7",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:1bbb91e1fb7034b8",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7293e870a8d5467f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"CASE 12 39MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative It was a clear, bright morning as the crew of a small passenger catamaran arrived on board to carry out their routine pre-sailing checks before their first trip of the day. While the master carried out his navigational aids checks, the mate went to the engine rooms and checked the fuel and main engines",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:25c0522a8c76df29",`source`:"shipkg:case:1f8ffc7c55c3",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:25c0522a8c76df29",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:8c30394060f9cd2e",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"30",`locator`:"PDF page 30",`quote`:"d, most likely, occurred gradually over a long period of time. 2.3.3 Pipework joints and shielding Whereas the main components of Pride of Canterbury’s CPP system were supplied after testing by the manufacturer, the interconnecting pipework was supplied and fitted by the shipyard when the vessel was constructed. Although the manufacturer’s drawings specified a particular type",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:27408755db4716c5",`source`:"shipkg:case:6f58fb8a8b17",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:27408755db4716c5",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:fe1c60aff6da4452",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"59",`locator`:"PDF page 59",`quote`:"52 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 22 Supper Would Have Been on Time if the Vessel Had Not Sunk Narrative A 24m steel hulled fishing trawler, with a crew of six, was fishing in calm seas when its engine began to make unusual noises. No-one was in the wheelhouse; the skipper, who was on watch, had gone to the mess room to prepare supper and the majority of the crew wer",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:28b886f51745046b",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:12275851bbd1",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:28b886f51745046b",`case_id`:"knowledge:coupling_failure",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:d3e64cd30311c1bb",`source_file`:"MAIB_2017_20_Hebrides_CPP_coupling.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/59b7ab1c40f0b61231e71a54/MAIBInvReport20_2017.pdf",`page`:"35",`locator`:"PDF page 35",`quote`:"s caused by the loosening of a setscrew used to attach a coupling to a stepper motor shaft due to its lack of rundown torque, the absence of thread locking fluid, and vibration during the actuator’s operation. [2.2] 3. The absence of service instructions for the actuator’s inspection and maintenance that were available from its manufacturer was pivotal to the failure. [2.3] 4. No thread l",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:30b6e05e8b368d8c",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:796439daaa03",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:30b6e05e8b368d8c",`case_id`:"knowledge:electrical_oscillation",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:d85a741773e8f8b9",`source_file`:"Frontiers_2021_marine_converter_oscillations.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/energy-research/articles/10.3389/fenrg.2020.529756/pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"sed in percentage terms. The limits are 0.5% for frequency and 5% for voltage. Well documented causes of such behavior include pulsating torque of generators’ prime movers and/or ﬂuctuating load, which combined with commonly used droop control method for load sharing, possibly leads to severe short and long-term frequency ﬂuctuations. However, little is known about the osci",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:33a067cb7a4b6b1d",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:ce7933999459",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:33a067cb7a4b6b1d",`case_id`:"knowledge:liner_scuffing",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:ec47f7f58361e500",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2016_633_piston_rings_scuffing.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-633.pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"to polishing and, possibly, smearing of the surface. When the liner surface is smeared, the open graphite lamel - las are closed making it difficult to keep a proper oil film. When the oil film is compromised, the cast iron piston rings, which are in contact with the cast iron liner, may generate high friction and seizures that will not recover (liner scuffing). During scuffing, the surface of the lin",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:386190211bd04886",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:6dbd0d51366c",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:386190211bd04886",`case_id`:"knowledge:bearing_electrical_erosion",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:9eb024fc4137b406",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN033_bearing_currents.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-033_C-Shaft-Bearing-Currents.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"aft within a rotating electrical machine - motor or alternator – to come under the influence of magnetic fields which result in a voltage (electrical pressure) generated along the axial length of the shaft. This ‘shaft voltage’ will then force current to flow from one end of the shaft, along a path which is radially out of the shaft through an end bracket continue along the alternators stator fra",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:38c71a0af58e42b5",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:660e09f63773",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:38c71a0af58e42b5",`case_id`:"knowledge:coolant_blockage",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1ac13d5b81e13593",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2016_623_cooling_water.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-623.pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"der head. The damages are often a result of corrosion, restrictions in or blocking of the cooling water flow, which are caused by deposits of limescale and/or rust. In general corrosion may result in leakages and thereby re - duce the lifetime and safety of the engine components. Lime- scale as well as rust deposits will reduce the heat transfer and may result in thermal overload of the com",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:3a7daa302187780c",`source`:"shipkg:case:d6e9f8f8ade2",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:3a7daa302187780c",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:eb8d9ba0db21fede",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"9",`locator`:"PDF page 9",`quote`:"ent and Incident Investigation Division and the engine manufacturer, MAN Diesel and Turbo SE. The investigation identified that a fracture of the connecting rod small end had led to the sudden failure of the main engine. The investigation also found that the method used to replace the connecting rod small end piston pin bearing bushes by the vessel manager’s maintenance support contractor had intr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:3d599eb3a886ff5a",`source`:"shipkg:case:63aa8b018e0d",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:3d599eb3a886ff5a",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:57049bc52d7488e2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"7",`locator`:"PDF page 7",`quote`:"mage to the port main engine room and rendered one of its four main engines inoperative for several weeks. The fire was caused by fuel leaking under pressure from the fuel system of main engine number 3 and igniting on an exposed hot surface. No one was injured and there was no pollution. The investigation found that the fuel had ignited on part of the engine’s exhaust system that had",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:44e6ad50114682ee",`source`:"shipkg:case:9792cd36162e",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:44e6ad50114682ee",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4e45851ecc9eb9f4",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"and no injuries. The MAIB investigation identified that the catastrophic damage to Windcat 8’s port main engine was caused by the failure of a piston connecting rod big end shell bearing, which resulted in the connecting rod assembly releasing and penetrating through the engine crankcase. The investigation also identified that: • A high oil temperature alarm prior to the engine failure warranted a more cautious a",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:47f51d2126c05caf",`source`:"shipkg:case:187dc871fbd5",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:47f51d2126c05caf",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:c3429f0fc22579e1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"e vessel’s heading. Given the weather conditions at the time, it is almost certain that Spirit of Discovery’s pitching caused the propellers to come out of the water. This caused a sudden reduction in torque on the propulsion motor and led to a very rapid increase in the motors’ rpm. The engine alarm and monitoring system recorded that, immediately before their shutdown, the rpm of each pod’s",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:4a52532339b893ff",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:84e503bec36b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:4a52532339b893ff",`case_id`:"knowledge:shaft_torsional",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1e17c52e491ed79c",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN235_torsional_analysis.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-235_A-Generating-Set-Assembly-Torsional-Vibration-Analysis.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"ng the extremely rapid pressure pulse of a burning air fuel mixture above the piston. The engine produces power in pulses and the pulses can excite very significant resonant responses. The pulsing of the power produced by the combustion process translates to angular vibrations in the crank shaft of the engine. The magnitude of the vibration depends on the number of cylinders in the engine. The movement of an i",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:4af0e99d2faed71b",`source`:"shipkg:case:6f58fb8a8b17",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:4af0e99d2faed71b",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:fe1c60aff6da4452",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url