e7f4ad",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:5d7a14186bd99b41",`case_id`:"knowledge:bearing_seizure",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:0523deba67297b7c",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2013_569_bearing_wear_monitoring.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2013-569.pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"C A main bearing damage was recently experienced on an MAN B&W S-MC-C main engine of medium bore size. The damage was caused by a sudden ingress of foreign matter into the bearing via the lubricating oil system, and it devel - oped rapidly into a bearing seizure. The engine was equipped with a bearing wear monitoring (BWM) system as recommended by MAN Diesel & Turbo (MDT). However, for rea",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:639a9a599f7a4918",`source`:"shipkg:case:d6e9f8f8ade2",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:639a9a599f7a4918",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:eb8d9ba0db21fede",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"9",`locator`:"PDF page 9",`quote`:"ent and Incident Investigation Division and the engine manufacturer, MAN Diesel and Turbo SE. The investigation identified that a fracture of the connecting rod small end had led to the sudden failure of the main engine. The investigation also found that the method used to replace the connecting rod small end piston pin bearing bushes by the vessel manager’s maintenance support contractor had intr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:67f79e2da375ba0b",`source`:"shipkg:case:1e6479e108d9",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:67f79e2da375ba0b",`case_id`:"kommandor_susan_dg1_2025",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:01f3913bd9c46899",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"f Forth, Scotland on 25 January 2025 SUMMARY At 1305 on 25 January 2025, the site investigation vessel Kommandor Susan suffered a catastrophic failure of a diesel generator engine while conducting sea trials in the Firth of Forth, Scotland. The failure resulted in an engine room fire and a complete power blackout. The crew responded promptly, extinguished the fire and mustered safely. The vessel lost propu",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:69d47ba823685724",`source`:"shipkg:case:551512d967af",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:69d47ba823685724",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:8b57dbab2f3af128",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"CASE 2 13MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative During passage, the duty engineer on board a ro-ro passenger ferry noticed an oily mist surrounding one of two air compressors (No1). The compressor in question was supplying control air to the vessel’s main engine clutches. The engineer changed over the supply of control air to a second compres",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:6d4af11b4be9e1e2",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:bff048b48ff1",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:6d4af11b4be9e1e2",`case_id`:"knowledge:generator_bearing_wear",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:65e2c4b3facd8c2b",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN076_alternator_bearings.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/2024-04/AGN076_C.pdf",`page`:"4",`locator`:"PDF page 4",`quote`:"t fail because of axial vibration, causing a fretting action in the housing, the cylindrical roller bearing might fail because of lack of grease or misalignment damage. The anti-friction ball bearings used on STAMFORD alternators are not insulated bearings. The design of STAMFORD alternators is such that the shaft does not come under the influence of magnetic fields that result in excessive vol",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:72203146f77ec8eb",`source`:"shipkg:case:9792cd36162e",`target`:"shipkg:system:5d1dca19fd66",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:72203146f77ec8eb",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4e45851ecc9eb9f4",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"and no injuries. The MAIB investigation identified that the catastrophic damage to Windcat 8’s port main engine was caused by the failure of a piston connecting rod big end shell bearing, which resulted in the connecting rod assembly releasing and penetrating through the engine crankcase. The investigation also identified that: • A high oil temperature alarm prior to the engine failure warranted a more cautious a",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:72aba66398325277",`source`:"shipkg:case:1e6479e108d9",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:72aba66398325277",`case_id`:"kommandor_susan_dg1_2025",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:01f3913bd9c46899",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"f Forth, Scotland on 25 January 2025 SUMMARY At 1305 on 25 January 2025, the site investigation vessel Kommandor Susan suffered a catastrophic failure of a diesel generator engine while conducting sea trials in the Firth of Forth, Scotland. The failure resulted in an engine room fire and a complete power blackout. The crew responded promptly, extinguished the fire and mustered safely. The vessel lost propu",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:73493089b1df8228",`source`:"shipkg:case:187dc871fbd5",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:73493089b1df8228",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:c3429f0fc22579e1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"e vessel’s heading. Given the weather conditions at the time, it is almost certain that Spirit of Discovery’s pitching caused the propellers to come out of the water. This caused a sudden reduction in torque on the propulsion motor and led to a very rapid increase in the motors’ rpm. The engine alarm and monitoring system recorded that, immediately before their shutdown, the rpm of each pod’s",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:7e9d424e9efc7234",`source`:"shipkg:case:1e6479e108d9",`target`:"shipkg:system:9bf053394931",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:7e9d424e9efc7234",`case_id`:"kommandor_susan_dg1_2025",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:01f3913bd9c46899",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"f Forth, Scotland on 25 January 2025 SUMMARY At 1305 on 25 January 2025, the site investigation vessel Kommandor Susan suffered a catastrophic failure of a diesel generator engine while conducting sea trials in the Firth of Forth, Scotland. The failure resulted in an engine room fire and a complete power blackout. The crew responded promptly, extinguished the fire and mustered safely. The vessel lost propu",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:80d458c65d231927",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:796439daaa03",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:80d458c65d231927",`case_id`:"knowledge:electrical_oscillation",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:d85a741773e8f8b9",`source_file`:"Frontiers_2021_marine_converter_oscillations.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/energy-research/articles/10.3389/fenrg.2020.529756/pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"sed in percentage terms. The limits are 0.5% for frequency and 5% for voltage. Well documented causes of such behavior include pulsating torque of generators’ prime movers and/or ﬂuctuating load, which combined with commonly used droop control method for load sharing, possibly leads to severe short and long-term frequency ﬂuctuations. However, little is known about the osci",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:8130d986a0df2efa",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:40cb53a64e31",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:8130d986a0df2efa",`case_id`:"knowledge:winding_insulation",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:31bd0a2dcc933aac",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN040_winding_insulation.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-040_E-Winding-Insulation-System.pdf",`page`:"6",`locator`:"PDF page 6",`quote`:"s of just a few MegOhms become more typical. Major factors, which affect and reduce the IR value, start with the winding outhang. Surface moisture, often present in conjunction with surface contamination, are typically the result of prevailing site conditions. Either will seriously reduce measured IR values, and if the root cause that allows this contaminant to be present i",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:81b01a91c8c6d199",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:8a35cec932af",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:81b01a91c8c6d199",`case_id`:"knowledge:damper_failure",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:71b1d838f3e59389",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2017_654_torsional_damper.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2017-654.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"oil - r educed lube oil supply - c ontaminated lube oil leading to carbon built up internal the damper b y the centrifugal forces will reduce the service life of the torsional vibration damper and may lead to failure before reaching the mentioned operation limits. Indications of a failing torsional vibration damper could be abnormal noise from the torsional vibration damper or any chan",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:8611ffcafe7de2fd",`source`:"shipkg:case:597875e258c6",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:8611ffcafe7de2fd",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:96829240b9d90823",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"19",`locator`:"PDF page 19",`quote`:"12 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 5 Propelled Onto the Berth Narrative A large roll-on roll-off passenger ferry, operating on its regular route between two European ports, suffered significant damage when it made heavy contact with a linkspan as it was being manoeuvred onto its berth. There were over 500 passengers and crew on board but no",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:8781522c263e23c5",`source`:"shipkg:case:00057f56fe39",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:8781522c263e23c5",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:19d0b2283f62b511",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"examination conducted by the vessel’s engine maker, Volvo Penta UK, concluded that the most probable trigger for the failure was debris in the engine’s oil channels following rebuild. The MAIB investigation established the following: • The engine had been completely rebuilt and failed after 5½ hours of operation. • The vessel’s soft patches 1 had not been removed, necessitating the engine to be lowered piecem",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:8c87932d5803d6a3",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:660e09f63773",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:8c87932d5803d6a3",`case_id`:"knowledge:coolant_blockage",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1ac13d5b81e13593",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2016_623_cooling_water.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-623.pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"der head. The damages are often a result of corrosion, restrictions in or blocking of the cooling water flow, which are caused by deposits of limescale and/or rust. In general corrosion may result in leakages and thereby re - duce the lifetime and safety of the engine components. Lime- scale as well as rust deposits will reduce the heat transfer and may result in thermal overload of the com",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:8f3f73c1c7b12d73",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:12275851bbd1",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:8f3f73c1c7b12d73",`case_id`:"knowledge:coupling_failure",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:d3e64cd30311c1bb",`source_file`:"MAIB_2017_20_Hebrides_CPP_coupling.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/59b7ab1c40f0b61231e71a54/MAIBInvReport20_2017.pdf",`page`:"35",`locator`:"PDF page 35",`quote`:"s caused by the loosening of a setscrew used to attach a coupling to a stepper motor shaft due to its lack of rundown torque, the absence of thread locking fluid, and vibration during the actuator’s operation. [2.2] 3. The absence of service instructions for the actuator’s inspection and maintenance that were available from its manufacturer was pivotal to the failure. [2.3] 4. No thread l",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:9215fd3e60167e1d",`source`:"shipkg:case:9676bd22b5e5",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`