: false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:9c51926f5fb93ee6",`source`:"shipkg:case:213f8edb92c2",`target`:"shipkg:system:9bf053394931",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:9c51926f5fb93ee6",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:af6ff177f229c6a2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e suppression spray heads were activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectric fluid vapour spr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:9c7571131c99cfed",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:6456485708ad",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:9c7571131c99cfed",`case_id`:"knowledge:shaft_generator_alignment",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:46c70849c9c28abc",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN039_marine_shaft_generators.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-039_C-Marine-Shaft-Generators.pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"When the shaft generator is aligned with the gearbox drive shaft, the ships design engineer must take great care to allow for the thermal expansion of the hot gearbox, which may well expand and lift the shaft centre line by < 1 mm. If the alignment is not accurate, then excessive vibration is likely to damage the shaft generator. There can also be lots of generator damaging vibration when the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:9cc5937f83460761",`source`:"shipkg:case:8b13bdb1a5bc",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:9cc5937f83460761",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:e1dce2948e24adc9",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"22 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 9 Sluggish Pitch Control Causes Serious Accident Narrative A chemical tanker was being manoeuvred to its designated jetty. As the vessel approached the quay, the pilot ordered an astern movement to enable a turn into the lock. The vessel did not respond and continued to proceed ahead. Despite placing the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:9f1f784fb8e94b71",`source`:"shipkg:case:1f8ffc7c55c3",`target`:"shipkg:system:5d1dca19fd66",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:9f1f784fb8e94b71",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:8c30394060f9cd2e",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"30",`locator`:"PDF page 30",`quote`:"d, most likely, occurred gradually over a long period of time. 2.3.3 Pipework joints and shielding Whereas the main components of Pride of Canterbury’s CPP system were supplied after testing by the manufacturer, the interconnecting pipework was supplied and fitted by the shipyard when the vessel was constructed. Although the manufacturer’s drawings specified a particular type",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:a5d0bf2917b2a861",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:40cb53a64e31",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:a5d0bf2917b2a861",`case_id`:"knowledge:winding_insulation",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:31bd0a2dcc933aac",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN040_winding_insulation.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-040_E-Winding-Insulation-System.pdf",`page`:"6",`locator`:"PDF page 6",`quote`:"s of just a few MegOhms become more typical. Major factors, which affect and reduce the IR value, start with the winding outhang. Surface moisture, often present in conjunction with surface contamination, are typically the result of prevailing site conditions. Either will seriously reduce measured IR values, and if the root cause that allows this contaminant to be present i",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:adfa5401a60945c3",`source`:"shipkg:case:9676bd22b5e5",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:adfa5401a60945c3",`case_id`:"sd2013_05_missing_filter",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7116308e5054c090",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"CASE 5 20 MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A fully loaded cargo ship departed port and proceeded on her voyage. Several days into the passage, the oil mist detector (OMD) on the medium speed diesel main engine alarmed. The duty engineer investigated but could not find any fault with the engine. He",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:af669d0519eb12fc",`source`:"shipkg:case:9792cd36162e",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:af669d0519eb12fc",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4e45851ecc9eb9f4",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"and no injuries. The MAIB investigation identified that the catastrophic damage to Windcat 8’s port main engine was caused by the failure of a piston connecting rod big end shell bearing, which resulted in the connecting rod assembly releasing and penetrating through the engine crankcase. The investigation also identified that: • A high oil temperature alarm prior to the engine failure warranted a more cautious a",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:b0859aec17e2a7be",`source`:"shipkg:case:8b13bdb1a5bc",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:b0859aec17e2a7be",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:e1dce2948e24adc9",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"22 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 9 Sluggish Pitch Control Causes Serious Accident Narrative A chemical tanker was being manoeuvred to its designated jetty. As the vessel approached the quay, the pilot ordered an astern movement to enable a turn into the lock. The vessel did not respond and continued to proceed ahead. Despite placing the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:b7bf394e390710c8",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:f8ea1aa17718",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:512427f592b7",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:b7bf394e390710c8",`case_id`:"knowledge:cooling_cavitation",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:2d4645410e75d447",`source_file`:"MAN_main_engine_auxiliary_efficiency.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/document-sync/efficiency-improvements-main-engine-auxiliary-systems-eng.pdf",`page`:"11",`locator`:"PDF page 11",`quote`:"ion and thereby increase cylinder wear. – Increased scavenge air temperature which will lead to increased fuel oil consumption. – A flow which is too low may cause local boiling on the water side inside the scavenge air cooler, which may lead to cavitation in the cooling water pipes. – The stated max. scavenge air temperature values given in the technical file may be exceeded, and the engine may thereby",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:bb9010c7f013b8b8",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:6dbd0d51366c",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:bb9010c7f013b8b8",`case_id`:"knowledge:bearing_electrical_erosion",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:9eb024fc4137b406",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN033_bearing_currents.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-033_C-Shaft-Bearing-Currents.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"aft within a rotating electrical machine - motor or alternator – to come under the influence of magnetic fields which result in a voltage (electrical pressure) generated along the axial length of the shaft. This ‘shaft voltage’ will then force current to flow from one end of the shaft, along a path which is radially out of the shaft through an end bracket continue along the alternators stator fra",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:bc128c07c9354ca4",`source`:"shipkg:case:278d7572ef08",`target`:"shipkg:system:5d1dca19fd66",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:bc128c07c9354ca4",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me4_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:3ca79df2a0332a1a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"igh levels of vibration, and contaminated lubricating oil might all have contributed to the event failure. [2.3.1] 3. Wight Sky’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:bedcac879f466798",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:84e503bec36b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:bedcac879f466798",`case_id`:"knowledge:shaft_torsional",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1e17c52e491ed79c",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN235_torsional_analysis.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-235_A-Generating-Set-Assembly-Torsional-Vibration-Analysis.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"ng the extremely rapid pressure pulse of a burning air fuel mixture above the piston. The engine produces power in pulses and the pulses can excite very significant resonant responses. The pulsing of the power produced by the combustion process translates to angular vibrations in the crank shaft of the engine. The magnitude of the vibration depends on the number of cylinders in the engine. The movement of an i",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c378845ae5e334a8",`source`:"shipkg:case:278d7572ef08",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c378845ae5e334a8",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me4_2018",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:3ca79df2a0332a1a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"igh levels of vibration, and contaminated lubricating oil might all have contributed to the event failure. [2.3.1] 3. Wight Sky’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c485b2af95e1ebc1",`source`:"shipkg:case:278d7572ef08",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c485b2af95e1ebc1",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me4_2018",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:3ca79df2a0332a1a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"igh levels of vibration, and contaminated lubricating oil might all have contributed to the event failure. [2.3.1] 3. Wight Sky’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c7bdc63e3eec79d6",`source`:"shipkg:case:213f8edb92c2",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c7bdc63e3eec79d6",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:af6ff177f229c6a2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e suppression spray heads were activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectric fluid vapour spr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:c89dff9ee6dba3b7",`source`:"shipkg:case:ad49b658b30b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:c89dff9ee6dba3b7",`case_id`:"sd2016_14_sea_valve",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:b7715f5c139d9453",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"33 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 14 Fail to Plan, Plan to Fail Narrative On a fine day, a general cargo vessel was on passage with a cargo of limestone. The master was on watch on the bridge. In the engine room, the chief engineer, motorman and a seaman were undertaking maintenance on one of the two main ballast pumps; the chief engineer",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cb7ed140bf8fa929",`source`:"shipkg:case:00057f56fe39",`target`:"shipkg:system:5d1dca19fd66",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:cb7ed140bf8fa929",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:19d0b2283f62b511",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"examination conducted by the vessel’s engine maker, Volvo Penta UK, concluded that the most probable trigger for the failure was debris in the engine’s oil channels following rebuild. The MAIB investigation established the following: • The engine had been completely rebuilt and failed after 5½ hours of operation. • The vessel’s soft patches 1 had not been removed, necessitating the engine to be lowered piecem",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:cc3fa7856e3a5b9a",`source`:"shipkg:case:7a1c0165bb56",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cc3fa7856e3a5b9a",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7e21ab64015c1360",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"19 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 8 Maintenance Induced Fire Narrative A fully loaded ro-ro passenger ferry was en route to its next port when the engineers in the control room acknowledged a low oil pressure alarm on one of the generators (Figure 1). On the CCTV they observed that oil from this generator was spraying on to the adjacen",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:ce4a0d48291ac815",`source`:"shipkg:case:7a1c0165bb56",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:ce4a0d48291ac815",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7e21ab64015c1360",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"19 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 8 Maintenance Induced Fire Narrative A fully loaded ro-ro passenger ferry was en route to its next port when the engineers in the control room acknowledged a low oil pressure alarm on one of the generators (Figure 1). On the CCTV they observed that oil from this generator was spraying on to the adjacen",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:cf3172f66abb4426",`source`:"shipkg:case:1e6479e108d9",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:cf3172f66abb4426",`case_id`:"kommandor_susan_dg1_2025",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:01f3913bd9c46899",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"f Forth, Scotland on 25 January 2025 SUMMARY At 1305 on 25 January 2025, the site investigation vessel Kommandor Susan suffered a catastrophic failure of a diesel generator engine while conducting sea trials in the Firth of Forth, Scotland. The failure resulted in an engine room fire and a complete power blackout. The crew responded promptly, extinguished the fire and mustered safely. The vessel lost propu",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:d9089e8a6dbbce0d",`source`:"shipkg:case:00057f56fe39",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:d9089e8a6dbbce0d",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:19d0b2283f62b511",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"examination conducted by the vessel’s engine maker, Volvo Penta UK, concluded that the most probable trigger for the failure was debris in the engine’s oil channels following rebuild. The MAIB investigation established the following: • The engine had been completely rebuilt and failed after 5½ hours of operation. • The vessel’s soft patches 1 had not been removed, necessitating the engine to be lowered piecem",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:da1de62ebf808696",`source`:"shipkg:case:63aa8b018e0d",`target`:"shipkg:system:5d1dca19fd66",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:da1de62ebf808696",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:57049bc52d7488e2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"7",`locator`:"PDF page 7",`quote`:"mage to the port main engine room and rendered one of its four main engines inoperative for several weeks. The fire was caused by fuel leaking under pressure from the fuel system of main engine number 3 and igniting on an exposed hot surface. No one was injured and there was no pollution. The investigation found that the fuel had ignited on part of the engine’s exhaust system that had",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:ddf470f0ec05af00",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:f8ea1aa17718",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:ddf470f0ec05af00",`case_id`:"knowledge:cooling_cavitation",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:2d4645410e75d447",`source_file`:"MAN_main_engine_auxiliary_efficiency.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/document-sync/efficiency-improvements-main-engine-auxiliary-systems-eng.pdf",`page`:"11",`locator`:"PDF page 11",`quote`:"ion and thereby increase cylinder wear. – Increased scavenge air temperature which will lead to increased fuel oil consumption. – A flow which is too low may cause local boiling on the water side inside the scavenge air cooler, which may lead to cavitation in the cooling water pipes. – The stated max. scavenge air temperature values given in the technical file may be exceeded, and the engine may thereby",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:ddfe38de303e54df",`source`:"shipkg:case:551512d967af",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:5e357a568055",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:ddfe38de303e54df",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:8b57dbab2f3af128",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"CASE 2 13MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative During passage, the duty engineer on board a ro-ro passenger ferry noticed an oily mist surrounding one of two air compressors (No1). The compressor in question was supplying control air to the vessel’s main engine clutches. The engineer changed over the supply of control air to a second compres",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e1453735667b9685",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:84e503bec36b",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e1453735667b9685",`case_id`:"knowledge:shaft_torsional",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:1e17c52e491ed79c",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN235_torsional_analysis.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-235_A-Generating-Set-Assembly-Torsional-Vibration-Analysis.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"ng the extremely rapid pressure pulse of a burning air fuel mixture above the piston. The engine produces power in pulses and the pulses can excite very significant resonant responses. The pulsing of the power produced by the combustion process translates to angular vibrations in the crank shaft of the engine. The magnitude of the vibration depends on the number of cylinders in the engine. The movement of an i",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e4bff73a42bdefa8",`source`:"shipkg:case:adf367a46f33",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e4bff73a42bdefa8",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me2_2018",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4846a9af2b7e6456",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"S 3.1 SAFETY ISSUES DIRECTLY CONTRIBUTING TO THE ACCIDENTS THAT HAVE BEEN ADDRESSED OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silic",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e681969faddd3784",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:bff048b48ff1",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e681969faddd3784",`case_id`:"knowledge:generator_bearing_wear",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:65e2c4b3facd8c2b",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN076_alternator_bearings.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/2024-04/AGN076_C.pdf",`page`:"4",`locator`:"PDF page 4",`quote`:"t fail because of axial vibration, causing a fretting action in the housing, the cylindrical roller bearing might fail because of lack of grease or misalignment damage. The anti-friction ball bearings used on STAMFORD alternators are not insulated bearings. The design of STAMFORD alternators is such that the shaft does not come under the influence of magnetic fields that result in excessive vol",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:e6ea05c9d949f8c2",`source`:"shipkg:case:597875e258c6",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:e6ea05c9d949f8c2",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:96829240b9d90823",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"19",`locator`:"PDF page 19",`quote`:"12 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 5 Propelled Onto the Berth Narrative A large roll-on roll-off passenger ferry, operating on its regular route between two European ports, suffered significant damage when it made heavy contact with a linkspan as it was being manoeuvred onto its berth. There were over 500 passengers and crew on board but no",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:ea2c70d8df227d3e",`source`:"shipkg:faulttype:ce7933999459",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:ea2c70d8df227d3e",`case_id`:"knowledge:liner_scuffing",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:ec47f7f58361e500",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2016_633_piston_rings_scuffing.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2016-633.pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"to polishing and, possibly, smearing of the surface. When the liner surface is smeared, the open graphite lamel - las are closed making it difficult to keep a proper oil film. When the oil film is compromised, the cast iron piston rings, which are in contact with the cast iron liner, may generate high friction and seizures that will not recover (liner scuffing). During scuffing, the surface of the lin",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:ead8467351a90af8",`source`:"shipkg:case:00057f56fe39",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:ead8467351a90af8",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:19d0b2283f62b511",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"examination conducted by the vessel’s engine maker, Volvo Penta UK, concluded that the most probable trigger for the failure was debris in the engine’s oil channels following rebuild. The MAIB investigation established the following: • The engine had been completely rebuilt and failed after 5½ hours of operation. • The vessel’s soft patches 1 had not been removed, necessitating the engine to be lowered piecem",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f5a05d14308ae52a",`source`:"shipkg:case:9792cd36162e",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:52e7560c8465",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f5a05d14308ae52a",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:4e45851ecc9eb9f4",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"and no injuries. The MAIB investigation identified that the catastrophic damage to Windcat 8’s port main engine was caused by the failure of a piston connecting rod big end shell bearing, which resulted in the connecting rod assembly releasing and penetrating through the engine crankcase. The investigation also identified that: • A high oil temperature alarm prior to the engine failure warranted a more cautious a",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:f8708991db8070bf",`source`:"shipkg:case:ffc594a9fab7",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:f8708991db8070bf",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7293e870a8d5467f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"CASE 12 39MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative It was a clear, bright morning as the crew of a small passenger catamaran arrived on board to carry out their routine pre-sailing checks before their first trip of the day. While the master carried out his navigational aids checks, the mate went to the engine rooms and checked the fuel and main engines",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:fb00168862e5f699",`source`:"shipkg:case:537a034e93e3",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:fb00168862e5f699",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:b840391c6c40b9b8",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"CASE 3 15MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A specialist cargo ship was in port loading a dangerous cargo. As a precaution, the vessel’s slow speed diesel main engine had been tested and was kept at a heightened state of readiness. This involved the fuel being shut off, the main engine indicator",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:fce2cc0d319e4881",`source`:"shipkg:case:7a1c0165bb56",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:4539c38d0a84",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:fce2cc0d319e4881",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:7e21ab64015c1360",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"19 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 8 Maintenance Induced Fire Narrative A fully loaded ro-ro passenger ferry was en route to its next port when the engineers in the control room acknowledged a low oil pressure alarm on one of the generators (Figure 1). On the CCTV they observed that oil from this generator was spraying on to the adjacen",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:fd16ad255f22091c",`source`:"shipkg:case:551512d967af",`target`:"shipkg:subsystem:d08eaf16cc46",`properties`:{`name`:"涉及系统",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`legacy_relation`:"IN_SUBSYSTEM",`id`:"edge:fd16ad255f22091c",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"curated_classification",`certainty_zh`:"研究者分类（非因果结论）",`evidence_id`:"ev:8b57dbab2f3af128",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"CASE 2 13MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative During passage, the duty engineer on board a ro-ro passenger ferry noticed an oily mist surrounding one of two air compressors (No1). The compressor in question was supplying control air to the vessel’s main engine clutches. The engineer changed over the supply of control air to a second compres",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"涉及系统\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false, \"legacy_relation\": \"IN_SUBSYSTEM\"}"}},{`id`:"edge:fd4ddfffcf5bc874",`source`:"shipkg:case:adf367a46f33",`target`:"shipkg:system:5d1dca19fd66",`properties`:{`name`:"采用系统架构",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:fd4ddfffcf5bc874",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me2_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4846a9af2b7e6456",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"S 3.1 SAFETY ISSUES DIRECTLY CONTRIBUTING TO THE ACCIDENTS THAT HAVE BEEN ADDRESSED OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silic",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"采用系统架构\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:IN_SYSTEM {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_25 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:00d23d64eeab966b",`source`:"shipkg:fault:2c644dcfc770",`target`:"shipkg:condition:ff44ed04fc9f",`properties`:{`name`:"很可能相关联",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:00d23d64eeab966b",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"probable",`certainty_zh`:"很可能",`evidence_id`:"ev:1143f5b1ae869724",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"9",`locator`:"PDF page 9",`quote`:"ation systems. Therefore, it is highly unlikely that the failure was the result of incorrect component assembly or a lack of oil. It is more likely that the failure was due to a weakness in the thin-walled shell bearing itself.",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"很可能相关联\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:0afb8ddaa0937ed2",`source`:"shipkg:condition:725f6ac0521d",`target`:"shipkg:fault:4de4eeb54341",`properties`:{`context_id`:"knowledge:electrical_oscillation",`knowledge_layer`:"reference",`data_origin`:"research_paper",`applicability`:"2021论文三类船舶的实测电网信号，含轴带发电化学品船；不是所有振荡都超限。DP船风浪影响主要作用于基波与频率，不能一概说风浪显著放大所有谐波。",`coupling_domains`:"机-电",`name`:"相关联",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:0afb8ddaa0937ed2",`case_id`:"knowledge:electrical_oscillation",`certainty`:"research_observation",`certainty_zh`:"论文实测观察（非本船已证实根因）",`evidence_id`:"ev:de200230bb22400e",`source_file`:"Frontiers_2021_marine_converter_oscillations.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/energy-research/articles/10.3389/fenrg.2020.529756/pdf",`page`:"6",`locator`:"PDF page 6",`quote`:"rd 45.1, 2017). Since the majority of loads had linear characteristic and did not vary, such a behavior is to be associated with power converter control under the condition of signi ﬁcantly varying frequency at the shaft generator terminal. Moreover, the level of all parameters oscillation was the highest of all analyzed ships. Research Onboard of Research-Training Ship The case study for the res",`props_json`:"{\"context_id\": \"knowledge:electrical_oscillation\", \"knowledge_layer\": \"reference\", \"data_origin\": \"research_paper\", \"applicability\": \"2021论文三类船舶的实测电网信号，含轴带发电化学品船；不是所有振荡都超限。DP船风浪影响主要作用于基波与频率，不能一概说风浪显著放大所有谐波。\", \"coupling_domains\": \"机-电\", \"name\": \"相关联\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:2683a3174de26882",`source`:"shipkg:symptom:ea2cdd59ea5c",`target`:"shipkg:fault:ce4fe75e21d8",`properties`:{`context_id`:"knowledge:bearing_seizure",`knowledge_layer`:"reference",`data_origin`:"manufacturer_guidance",`applicability`:"主机滑动轴承；烧瓦是检索用的工程统称，不能把全部轴瓦疲劳、瓦片转位或轴承失效直接标成已证实烧瓦。",`coupling_domains`:"热-机",`name`:"相关联",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:2683a3174de26882",`case_id`:"knowledge:bearing_seizure",`certainty`:"guidance",`certainty_zh`:"厂家一般机理/指导（须核对机型）",`evidence_id`:"ev:06bb917f36e1db67",`source_file`:"MAN_SL2013_569_bearing_wear_monitoring.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.man-es.com/docs/default-source/service-letters/sl2013-569.pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"BWM system. • 58 minutes passed from the initial stage of the seizure until the alarm set off and slow-down was requested by the OMD system. The BWM specification issued by MDT was updated in 2011 to enable early detection of a sudden and rapidly Fig. 2: Sequence of alarms developing damage like the one mentioned above. The system fitted to the engine in question was",`props_json`:"{\"context_id\": \"knowledge:bearing_seizure\", \"knowledge_layer\": \"reference\", \"data_origin\": \"manufacturer_guidance\", \"applicability\": \"主机滑动轴承；烧瓦是检索用的工程统称，不能把全部轴瓦疲劳、瓦片转位或轴承失效直接标成已证实烧瓦。\", \"coupling_domains\": \"热-机\", \"name\": \"相关联\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:7c4eca2a004acf93",`source`:"shipkg:condition:dc209dc61e12",`target`:"shipkg:condition:37396a158a92",`properties`:{`context_id`:"knowledge:shaft_generator_alignment",`knowledge_layer`:"reference",`data_origin`:"manufacturer_guidance",`applicability`:"通过齿轮箱及联轴器驱动的轴带发电机；不能推广到所有同轴无附加轴承的构型。",`coupling_domains`:"热-机-电",`name`:"相关联",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:7c4eca2a004acf93",`case_id`:"knowledge:shaft_generator_alignment",`certainty`:"guidance",`certainty_zh`:"厂家一般机理/指导（须核对机型）",`evidence_id`:"ev:46c70849c9c28abc",`source_file`:"STAMFORD_AGN039_marine_shaft_generators.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.stamford-avk.com/sites/stamfordavk/files/AGNs/AGN-039_C-Marine-Shaft-Generators.pdf",`page`:"2",`locator`:"PDF page 2",`quote`:"When the shaft generator is aligned with the gearbox drive shaft, the ships design engineer must take great care to allow for the thermal expansion of the hot gearbox, which may well expand and lift the shaft centre line by < 1 mm. If the alignment is not accurate, then excessive vibration is likely to damage the shaft generator. There can also be lots of generator damaging vibration when the",`props_json`:"{\"context_id\": \"knowledge:shaft_generator_alignment\", \"knowledge_layer\": \"reference\", \"data_origin\": \"manufacturer_guidance\", \"applicability\": \"通过齿轮箱及联轴器驱动的轴带发电机；不能推广到所有同轴无附加轴承的构型。\", \"coupling_domains\": \"热-机-电\", \"name\": \"相关联\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:9330596fd95bc73d",`source`:"shipkg:condition:5d3ac9abb37a",`target`:"shipkg:fault:72c71c94ca13",`properties`:{`name`:"相关联",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:9330596fd95bc73d",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:383cc33975e2e37e",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"60",`locator`:"PDF page 60",`quote`:"sank suggests the failure of a main engine sea water cooling pipe. Analysis of maintenance records showed that this pipework had not been inspected or renewed for many years. Sea inlet pipework should be thoroughly checked during planned maintenance periods. skipper, who had remained in the wheelhouse, then broadcast a “Mayday” message on VHF radio, which was received and relayed by the coastguard to",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"相关联\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:ASSOCIATED_WITH {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_26 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:01fc144895cef73d",`source`:"shipkg:fault:a20cef558a0a",`target`:"shipkg:component:2a19cfd5c18a",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:01fc144895cef73d",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me4_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:45cb3bc7993a557f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"y’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the metal-to-metal contact between surfaces of the connecting rods and their bearing caps. This would have caused fr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:096efa24a969e938",`source`:"shipkg:fault:40958d8dddba",`target`:"shipkg:component:0dcadce61c82",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:096efa24a969e938",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:9c5f7101c8442b54",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"15",`locator`:"PDF page 15",`quote`:"essel was able to berth safely alongside, assisted by harbour tugs. Subsequent investigation identified that No2 compressor had a damaged discharge valve. Neither compressor had been able to keep up with demand.",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:192176bf64b44fd8",`source`:"shipkg:fault:cdf116929c39",`target`:"shipkg:component:160bdfff5e4e",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:192176bf64b44fd8",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:818a140783772a9b",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"43",`locator`:"PDF page 43",`quote`:"iple this was an entirely sensible precaution to protect the high voltage pod motor from damage. However, the low position of the bilge sensor meant that it could be activated by a relatively small amount of liquid that accumulated within the pod. Since the bilge suction probably did not extend low enough for the automatic bilge pumps to effectively pump the water out,",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:1b6014b7d03ff82b",`source`:"shipkg:fault:439f73a406a0",`target`:"shipkg:component:46d84bd3b794",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:1b6014b7d03ff82b",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:f4e14e047a77ffb2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"n by the engineer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage to the shaft and gearing (Figure 1) and to the turning gear casing (Figure 2) disabled the ship for a month and cost a six-figure sum to repair. To Turn",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:1c7edb137cc82c49",`source`:"shipkg:fault:2c644dcfc770",`target`:"shipkg:component:8052e7754d5f",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:1c7edb137cc82c49",`case_id`:"kommandor_susan_dg1_2025",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e32631e4946436ab",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"5",`locator`:"PDF page 5",`quote`:"rod cap number six comes off. Pon Power’s report concluded that: With the facts gathered the most likely root cause is failure of connecting rod bearing number five. The excessive wear on the other connecting rod bearings show that the most likely root cause for the bearing failure is weak bonding of the copper layer. Evidence of weak material bonding was found in several bearings (Figure 4)",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:2e10fd82cbcb1ef5",`source`:"shipkg:fault:aba0717d72a0",`target`:"shipkg:component:45c063af0c7c",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:2e10fd82cbcb1ef5",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:1637d85df75c53f0",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"cluded that: ○ Debris in the engine’s oil channels was most probably responsible for initiating the failure. ○ When the shells of main bearing 5 turned, the lubrication supply to big end bearing 4 was blocked, resulting in destructive failure. • Rebuilding the engine in a clean and controlled environment and transferring it complete into the engine room would have reduced",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:41c38630e54eb5b6",`source`:"shipkg:fault:2c644dcfc770",`target`:"shipkg:component:3552bc595328",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:41c38630e54eb5b6",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:ff3253f5416e42be",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"es. The MAIB investigation identified that the catastrophic damage to Windcat 8’s port main engine was caused by the failure of a piston connecting rod big end shell bearing, which resulted in the connecting rod assembly releasing and penetrating through the engine crankcase. The investigation also identified that: • A high oil temperature alarm prior to the engine failure warranted a more cautious a",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:4992dedca65165a2",`source`:"shipkg:fault:ae4a492efe41",`target`:"shipkg:component:d16e663b1271",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:4992dedca65165a2",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:470e8782d7a79377",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"t in the starboard CPP system, onto the hot exhaust uptakes of the starboard main engines. The flanged joint ruptured because the CPP system became over- pressurised as a result of the back pressure valve (PSV3) becoming jammed in the closed position. The reason for the temporary increase in the starboard main engine load to 100% and corresponding increase in turbocharger rpm has not been det",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:59c4a68230fbe396",`source`:"shipkg:fault:72c71c94ca13",`target`:"shipkg:component:a53bfe23945e",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:59c4a68230fbe396",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e235f3eb9480640d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"60",`locator`:"PDF page 60",`quote`:"al. Never delay unnecessarily when abandoning a sinking ship. 4. The rate of water ingress and the speed at which the vessel sank suggests the failure of a main engine sea water cooling pipe. Analysis of maintenance records showed that this pipework had not been inspected or renewed for many years. Sea inlet pipework should be thoroughly checked during planned maintenance periods. skipper, who had remained in the whe",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:5b39376c40628993",`source`:"shipkg:fault:4cb7be531584",`target`:"shipkg:component:6f0aead2b5a6",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:5b39376c40628993",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4f930aa49cf38734",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"ch went according to plan until the ferry was about 1½ ships’ length from its final berthing position, when her three main engine clutches disengaged almost simultaneously. No Air, No Clutch, No CPP , No Brakes Damage to lubrication oil pipe and bottom end bearing Bottom end bearing Failed lubricant oil pipe end fitting",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:5fc9dfa91d77c020",`source`:"shipkg:fault:e97eee073fc6",`target`:"shipkg:component:1157de5d43da",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:5fc9dfa91d77c020",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e2523ed63e0b4019",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"at Spirit of Discovery’s pitching caused the propellers to come out of the water. This caused a sudden reduction in torque on the propulsion motor and led to a very rapid increase in the motors’ rpm. The engine alarm and monitoring system recorded that, immediately before their shutdown, the rpm of each pod’s propulsion motor very rapidly increased and exceeded the preset o",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:602eace28bff4b46",`source`:"shipkg:fault:2ac2de665aa1",`target`:"shipkg:component:960fe73dbb4b",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:602eace28bff4b46",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:8e948de9b710ce4f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"ond compressor (No2) and reported his actions to the senior engineer in the ECR. Immediate investigation identified that the main lubricating oil discharge pipe assembly in No1 compressor had detached, and that the bottom end bearing had overheated and failed (see figure). No1 compressor was isolated but the engineers soon noticed that the air pressure in the main air receiver was dropping. Short",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:6331da034bd8f903",`source`:"shipkg:fault:f078b5a27275",`target`:"shipkg:component:ca5637067a12",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:6331da034bd8f903",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:5a827f088fee8abd",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"19",`locator`:"PDF page 19",`quote`:"er being dimmed overnight, the master attempted to adjust the brightness. Distracted by a conversation with the chief officer, he pressed the wrong button (Figure 1) and inadvertently switched the vessel’s starboard controllable pitch propeller (CPP) from its normal control mode to its back-up mode. The error was not spotted by the master or his bridge team as they continued toward",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:703e5ecaa2681b88",`source`:"shipkg:fault:f2f9d4b10a0b",`target`:"shipkg:component:4d8f23e8a303",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:703e5ecaa2681b88",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:3749ce726e3d4dcc",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"before it was able to spread. No one was hurt in the incident. Subsequent investigation revealed that: • The oil had come from a loose plug on the generator’s engine-mounted lubricating oil pump (Figure 2a). This had vibrated loose as a result of it being insufficiently tightened by shore staff during a recent dry dock. • A section of the adjacent generator’s exhaust piping had been left unlagged following its overhaul d",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:73983c5041ea7c30",`source`:"shipkg:fault:b7f3d0b1bf24",`target`:"shipkg:component:828d4178b93f",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:73983c5041ea7c30",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:1abb50030379f9ee",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"rag, which he casually left on a tank top above the engine exhaust manifold. Vibration caused the oil-soaked rag to fall onto the hot manifold and catch fire. The small fire then ignited the engine high temperature alarm cabling loom, causing it to short circuit and set off the alarm in the wheelhouse (Figure 2). The functional fire and smoke alarm sensors were some distance from the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:73f0fbdb8432f014",`source`:"shipkg:fault:1e5a23a200ad",`target`:"shipkg:component:fd37cf4aeb64",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:73f0fbdb8432f014",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:cd6c3c8ec42fee37",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"27",`locator`:"PDF page 27",`quote`:"ended to release at 6-8 bar, released at much greater pressures, ranging from 20 to 77 bar. When dismantled it was found that the piston was worn, allowing it to tilt and stick sporadically. The valve supplier considered the amount of wear was normal given its 23 years of service. The pressure safety valve (PSV1) was also dismantled and found to be worn, but to a much lesser extent. 1.12 SIMILAR ACCIDEN",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:78663b40c46179a3",`source`:"shipkg:fault:4e2929b80b35",`target`:"shipkg:component:c3d265fa990c",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:78663b40c46179a3",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:5e9210d8dbe9bf48",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"9",`locator`:"PDF page 9",`quote`:"Investigation Division and the engine manufacturer, MAN Diesel and Turbo SE. The investigation identified that a fracture of the connecting rod small end had led to the sudden failure of the main engine. The investigation also found that the method used to replace the connecting rod small end piston pin bearing bushes by the vessel manager’s maintenance support contractor had intr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:80cfc3d350b9d643",`source`:"shipkg:fault:8027eb707475",`target`:"shipkg:component:6432d2482f06",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:80cfc3d350b9d643",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:157ede421b19ee3a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"neer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage to the shaft and gearing (Figure 1) and to the turning gear casing (Figure 2) disabled the ship for a month and cost a six-figure sum to repair. To Turn or Not to Turn?",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:9bf92f367d2100f8",`source`:"shipkg:fault:c44e6c4545bf",`target`:"shipkg:component:282dcd34a768",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:9bf92f367d2100f8",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:a33dab8e3476ce99",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"20",`locator`:"PDF page 20",`quote`:"tarboard CPP back-up control mode was inadvertently selected, the master lost bridge control of that propeller. The starboard CPP continued to thrust at over half ahead throughout the vessel’s approach to the berth and up until its engine was stopped (about 2 hours after the contact). Starboard pitch back-up on/off control button Centre console lamps dimmer control buttons Figure 1: Part of brid",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:9f193d4cada42c87",`source`:"shipkg:fault:fce2f501a499",`target`:"shipkg:component:3295e52dd075",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:9f193d4cada42c87",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:dc67d8904baddd49",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"led, but fortunately the damage was above the waterline (Figure 1). The subsequent investigation identified that the vessel had a history of sluggish astern response. However, the crew had accepted this as a ‘characteristic’ of the vessel and usually compensated for it by demanding astern movements well in advance. The CPP control panel on the bridge had a back-up control button (Figure 2) fo",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:a310428762de6253",`source`:"shipkg:fault:58d32c38d0ac",`target`:"shipkg:component:784cd78efb12",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:a310428762de6253",`case_id`:"sd2013_05_missing_filter",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:b10e854dd960072c",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"ate without any problems and the vessel undertook several voyages. However, after the engine failure, the duplex filter was found without a filter cartridge in the on-line filter chamber, and the engine lubricating oil system was contaminated. The contamination caused main bearing seizure, the rotation of bearing shells and the blockage of oil ways, and subsequent oil starvation and",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:b2a661a026da52ad",`source`:"shipkg:fault:dd6aba2caf5a",`target`:"shipkg:component:ed0a2ad1e065",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:b2a661a026da52ad",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:504217846ee2ac5f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"oil, from a ruptured pipework joint in the starboard CPP system, onto the hot exhaust uptakes of the starboard main engines. The flanged joint ruptured because the CPP system became over- pressurised as a result of the back pressure valve (PSV3) becoming jammed in the closed position. The reason for the temporary increase in the starboard main engine load to 100% and correspondi",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:bc74a4ad474e6f70",`source`:"shipkg:fault:7b886d9d51c3",`target`:"shipkg:component:e0a03cf176fe",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:bc74a4ad474e6f70",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:861eb8fbe47cd585",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"f pressurised fuel. The fuel sprayed onto the exposed exhaust manifold that was operating at a temperature exceeding 220°C when a screw in a two-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by anti-splashing tape or shielding and fuel was able to escape forcefully. [2.3.2] 3. Th",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:be3809f5644484fb",`source`:"shipkg:fault:b2aa91be158b",`target`:"shipkg:component:29dfcfe886de",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:be3809f5644484fb",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:800bdca6cdc9fb5d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"64",`locator`:"PDF page 64",`quote`:"e arly w arning t o p revent mo re s erious problems. 2.4.5 Current imbalance detection system The capacitor exploded because the inoperative imbalance detection system could not identify the deterioration of the capacitors. The failure of the imbalance system’s current transformer remained undetected for what could have been several years. It is certain that this system was not working in 2008",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:beabaef04fb923c1",`source`:"shipkg:fault:6ade8daa881a",`target`:"shipkg:component:1333df9ac9f2",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:beabaef04fb923c1",`case_id`:"sd2013_05_missing_filter",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:82256a9ee8fd56dd",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"d main bearing journals; overheating of the bedplate at the main bearing housings; overheating of the piston connecting rods; the seizure of several pistons (Figure 2); failure of the camshaft and turbo charger bearings, and metallic debris throughout the lubricating oil system. The damage sustained necessitated an engine rebuild and the replacement of the bedplate and crankshaft. A",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:c69be45f369aa908",`source`:"shipkg:fault:020786dc9fd0",`target`:"shipkg:component:864e3371e086",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:c69be45f369aa908",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e9d71048b791d31a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"as a result of it being insufficiently tightened by shore staff during a recent dry dock. • A section of the adjacent generator’s exhaust piping had been left unlagged following its overhaul during the recent dry dock (Figure 2b). This was hidden from view by the exhaust casing. • Fine oil spray ignited when it came into contact with the hot exhaust casing. Figure 1: Location of the generator w",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:c86afda0091fbc18",`source`:"shipkg:fault:256ba55c5fb2",`target`:"shipkg:component:a85d6cb18c5c",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:c86afda0091fbc18",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:2d2994aad520a17a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"MMENDATIONS 1. Stena Europe experienced a fire on one of its main engines due to an uncontrolled release of pressurised fuel. The fuel sprayed onto the exposed exhaust manifold that was operating at a temperature exceeding 220°C when a screw in a two-screw flange within the fuel oil pipework loosened. [2.2] 2. The fuel oil spray was allowed to reach the hot surface because the joint was not protected by",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:c92d57e440182816",`source`:"shipkg:fault:aba0717d72a0",`target`:"shipkg:component:be4ab56339d8",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:c92d57e440182816",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me2_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:0b7a42308cc8b6cc",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"D OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silica sand and other abrasive particles embe",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:c9a8accfa0a99686",`source`:"shipkg:fault:c1ffab11185c",`target`:"shipkg:component:5fbf5f22d00c",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:c9a8accfa0a99686",`case_id`:"sd2016_14_sea_valve",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:2180f44fb45d636d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"ssel. Are you prepared for a flooding emergency? 3. Examination of the isolating valve following the accident identified that the valve actuator had been defective, giving an impression that the valve was fully closed when it was not. Although there was a visual indicator located on the side of the actuator, this was not checked to confirm that the valve was closed prior to removal of the f",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:da74d2079434ce93",`source`:"shipkg:fault:5737f3610967",`target`:"shipkg:component:726d763bfec1",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:da74d2079434ce93",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e1952d272da22996",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"ere activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectric fluid vapour spr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:db41a9ebd79d7f4d",`source`:"shipkg:fault:15fa82225a89",`target`:"shipkg:component:28a67e535633",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:db41a9ebd79d7f4d",`case_id`:"sd2016_14_sea_valve",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:a815947a42cdaece",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"seaman rigged the portable electric water pump on the main deck but, with the vessel now running on emergency power only, he was unable to start the pump. The master contacted the coastguard by VHF radio and advised that the vessel was flooding. The coastguard transmitted a “Mayday Relay”, and RNLI lifeboats from two stations were tasked to assist along with a Royal Navy helicopte",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:e08960eb7eecab46",`source`:"shipkg:fault:ce4fe75e21d8",`target`:"shipkg:component:67b7bcd7344e",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:e08960eb7eecab46",`case_id`:"sd2013_05_missing_filter",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:df67722cb172233f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"filter cartridge in the on-line filter chamber, and the engine lubricating oil system was contaminated. The contamination caused main bearing seizure, the rotation of bearing shells and the blockage of oil ways, and subsequent oil starvation and overheating to other bearings and to the pistons. The engine daily logs referred to oil filter cartridge changes only prior to the re",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:f505f5cce7847083",`source`:"shipkg:fault:999defd690d8",`target`:"shipkg:component:26867a3d02f0",`properties`:{`name`:"影响部件",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:f505f5cce7847083",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:188654e8f7b787d6",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"ked rag to fall onto the hot manifold and catch fire. The small fire then ignited the engine high temperature alarm cabling loom, causing it to short circuit and set off the alarm in the wheelhouse (Figure 2). The functional fire and smoke alarm sensors were some distance from the fire, and the smoke and heat had not migrated that far by the time the master noticed the smoke on the ca",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"影响部件\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:AFFECTS_COMPONENT {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_27 }
