CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:19940803c75a7df5",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:32aaec3208ad",`target`:"shipkg:case:ffc594a9fab7",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:19940803c75a7df5",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:7293e870a8d5467f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"CASE 12 39MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative It was a clear, bright morning as the crew of a small passenger catamaran arrived on board to carry out their routine pre-sailing checks before their first trip of the day. While the master carried out his navigational aids checks, the mate went to the engine rooms and checked the fuel and main engines",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:3372e243650d990c",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:a81974e78c4c",`target`:"shipkg:case:ad49b658b30b",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:3372e243650d990c",`case_id`:"sd2016_14_sea_valve",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:b7715f5c139d9453",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"40",`locator`:"PDF page 40",`quote`:"33 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 14 Fail to Plan, Plan to Fail Narrative On a fine day, a general cargo vessel was on passage with a cargo of limestone. The master was on watch on the bridge. In the engine room, the chief engineer, motorman and a seaman were undertaking maintenance on one of the two main ballast pumps; the chief engineer",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:3387676e26c9f1cc",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:fa10fa0f80d3",`target`:"shipkg:case:278d7572ef08",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:3387676e26c9f1cc",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me4_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:3ca79df2a0332a1a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"igh levels of vibration, and contaminated lubricating oil might all have contributed to the event failure. [2.3.1] 3. Wight Sky’s ME4 failed catastrophically because of an assembly error during build at Volvo Penta’s factory in Sweden. Two of the engine’s matched connecting rod big end bearing caps had been transposed during the engine assembly process. [2.3.2] 4. The transposition of the bearing caps reduced the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:3ca82b731174c223",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:3fb5a9c954ef",`target`:"shipkg:case:7a1c0165bb56",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:3ca82b731174c223",`case_id`:"sd2016_08_generator_oil",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:7e21ab64015c1360",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"26",`locator`:"PDF page 26",`quote`:"19 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 8 Maintenance Induced Fire Narrative A fully loaded ro-ro passenger ferry was en route to its next port when the engineers in the control room acknowledged a low oil pressure alarm on one of the generators (Figure 1). On the CCTV they observed that oil from this generator was spraying on to the adjacen",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:46fa980554b1dcb7",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:ce08d017f5c9",`target`:"shipkg:case:9792cd36162e",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:46fa980554b1dcb7",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4e45851ecc9eb9f4",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"and no injuries. The MAIB investigation identified that the catastrophic damage to Windcat 8’s port main engine was caused by the failure of a piston connecting rod big end shell bearing, which resulted in the connecting rod assembly releasing and penetrating through the engine crankcase. The investigation also identified that: • A high oil temperature alarm prior to the engine failure warranted a more cautious a",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:62105b1b63c965d1",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:5d3e7e7eb367",`target`:"shipkg:case:537a034e93e3",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:62105b1b63c965d1",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:b840391c6c40b9b8",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"CASE 3 15MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A specialist cargo ship was in port loading a dangerous cargo. As a precaution, the vessel’s slow speed diesel main engine had been tested and was kept at a heightened state of readiness. This involved the fuel being shut off, the main engine indicator",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:68dbd2748e6de55c",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:db8f8f17b349",`target`:"shipkg:case:d6e9f8f8ade2",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:68dbd2748e6de55c",`case_id`:"finlandia_seaways_me_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:eb8d9ba0db21fede",`source_file`:"MAIB_2021_02_Finlandia_Seaways_connecting_rod_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-ro-ro-cargo-vessel-finlandia-seaways-with-1-person-injured",`page`:"9",`locator`:"PDF page 9",`quote`:"ent and Incident Investigation Division and the engine manufacturer, MAN Diesel and Turbo SE. The investigation identified that a fracture of the connecting rod small end had led to the sudden failure of the main engine. The investigation also found that the method used to replace the connecting rod small end piston pin bearing bushes by the vessel manager’s maintenance support contractor had intr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:69d1b0f047210221",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:e9a9185f76f9",`target`:"shipkg:case:551512d967af",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:69d1b0f047210221",`case_id`:"sd2013_02_control_air",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:8b57dbab2f3af128",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"CASE 2 13MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative During passage, the duty engineer on board a ro-ro passenger ferry noticed an oily mist surrounding one of two air compressors (No1). The compressor in question was supplying control air to the vessel’s main engine clutches. The engineer changed over the supply of control air to a second compres",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:800b300fcff167a1",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:808ea34d5772",`target`:"shipkg:case:597875e258c6",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:800b300fcff167a1",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:96829240b9d90823",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"19",`locator`:"PDF page 19",`quote`:"12 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 5 Propelled Onto the Berth Narrative A large roll-on roll-off passenger ferry, operating on its regular route between two European ports, suffered significant damage when it made heavy contact with a linkspan as it was being manoeuvred onto its berth. There were over 500 passengers and crew on board but no",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:8187c11f67a30611",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:fa10fa0f80d3",`target`:"shipkg:case:00057f56fe39",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:8187c11f67a30611",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:19d0b2283f62b511",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"examination conducted by the vessel’s engine maker, Volvo Penta UK, concluded that the most probable trigger for the failure was debris in the engine’s oil channels following rebuild. The MAIB investigation established the following: • The engine had been completely rebuilt and failed after 5½ hours of operation. • The vessel’s soft patches 1 had not been removed, necessitating the engine to be lowered piecem",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:8942987f1ce37075",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:3cb736742ac6",`target`:"shipkg:case:213f8edb92c2",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:8942987f1ce37075",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:af6ff177f229c6a2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e suppression spray heads were activated, one in the aft harmonic filter room and the other in the aft main switchboard room. The explosion was triggered by deterioration in the capacitors in the aft HF . Internal arcing between the capacitor plates developed, which vaporised the dielectric medium causing the internal pressure to increase, until it caused the capacitor casing to rupture. Dielectric fluid vapour spr",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:97738208d5370376",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:ea737bd37b3c",`target`:"shipkg:case:6f58fb8a8b17",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:97738208d5370376",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:fe1c60aff6da4452",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"59",`locator`:"PDF page 59",`quote`:"52 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 22 Supper Would Have Been on Time if the Vessel Had Not Sunk Narrative A 24m steel hulled fishing trawler, with a crew of six, was fishing in calm seas when its engine began to make unusual noises. No-one was in the wheelhouse; the skipper, who was on watch, had gone to the mess room to prepare supper and the majority of the crew wer",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:b0a7b8cd30d6fc97",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:fa10fa0f80d3",`target`:"shipkg:case:adf367a46f33",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:b0a7b8cd30d6fc97",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me2_2018",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4846a9af2b7e6456",`source_file`:"MAIB_2022_04_Wight_Sky_multiple_engine_failures.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6267cc85e90e071690c1b679/2022-4-WightSky-Report.pdf",`page`:"84",`locator`:"PDF page 84",`quote`:"S 3.1 SAFETY ISSUES DIRECTLY CONTRIBUTING TO THE ACCIDENTS THAT HAVE BEEN ADDRESSED OR RESULTED IN RECOMMENDATIONS 1. Wight Sky’s ME2 failed catastrophically due to a sudden loss of lubricating oil supply to its number five main journal bearing and number four crankpin. [2.3.1] 2. The oilway to the main journal and crankpin was blocked off when the bearing shells turned in their housing. Poor fuel combustion, the presence of silic",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:b6bc3f8a3d0ccec3",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:5466bfcfc864",`target`:"shipkg:case:187dc871fbd5",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:b6bc3f8a3d0ccec3",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:c3429f0fc22579e1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"e vessel’s heading. Given the weather conditions at the time, it is almost certain that Spirit of Discovery’s pitching caused the propellers to come out of the water. This caused a sudden reduction in torque on the propulsion motor and led to a very rapid increase in the motors’ rpm. The engine alarm and monitoring system recorded that, immediately before their shutdown, the rpm of each pod’s",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:c3ad4a1a4e545e67",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:2ed46421a269",`target`:"shipkg:case:1f8ffc7c55c3",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:c3ad4a1a4e545e67",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:8c30394060f9cd2e",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"30",`locator`:"PDF page 30",`quote`:"d, most likely, occurred gradually over a long period of time. 2.3.3 Pipework joints and shielding Whereas the main components of Pride of Canterbury’s CPP system were supplied after testing by the manufacturer, the interconnecting pipework was supplied and fitted by the shipyard when the vessel was constructed. Although the manufacturer’s drawings specified a particular type",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:cdb206943226e856",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:e9dd95119f56",`target`:"shipkg:case:8b13bdb1a5bc",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:cdb206943226e856",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e1dce2948e24adc9",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"22 MAIB Safety Digest 1/2016 CASE 9 Sluggish Pitch Control Causes Serious Accident Narrative A chemical tanker was being manoeuvred to its designated jetty. As the vessel approached the quay, the pilot ordered an astern movement to enable a turn into the lock. The vessel did not respond and continued to proceed ahead. Despite placing the",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:d1a33046210e8c90",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:205954d6d86e",`target`:"shipkg:case:9676bd22b5e5",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:d1a33046210e8c90",`case_id`:"sd2013_05_missing_filter",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:7116308e5054c090",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"CASE 5 20 MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 Narrative A fully loaded cargo ship departed port and proceeded on her voyage. Several days into the passage, the oil mist detector (OMD) on the medium speed diesel main engine alarmed. The duty engineer investigated but could not find any fault with the engine. He",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:dbb7fc5be3025318",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:2ee30864aa2d",`target`:"shipkg:case:1e6479e108d9",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:dbb7fc5be3025318",`case_id`:"kommandor_susan_dg1_2025",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:01f3913bd9c46899",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_10_Kommandor_Susan_generator_bearing_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/catastrophic-engine-failure-and-subsequent-fire-on-board-the-site-investigation-vessel-kommandor-susan",`page`:"1",`locator`:"PDF page 1",`quote`:"f Forth, Scotland on 25 January 2025 SUMMARY At 1305 on 25 January 2025, the site investigation vessel Kommandor Susan suffered a catastrophic failure of a diesel generator engine while conducting sea trials in the Firth of Forth, Scotland. The failure resulted in an engine room fire and a complete power blackout. The crew responded promptly, extinguished the fire and mustered safely. The vessel lost propu",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:dbf24fe0f3995583",`source`:"shipkg:vessel:9f37ba0a1a27",`target`:"shipkg:case:63aa8b018e0d",`properties`:{`name`:"发生案例",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:dbf24fe0f3995583",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:57049bc52d7488e2",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"7",`locator`:"PDF page 7",`quote`:"mage to the port main engine room and rendered one of its four main engines inoperative for several weeks. The fire was caused by fuel leaking under pressure from the fuel system of main engine number 3 and igniting on an exposed hot surface. No one was injured and there was no pollution. The investigation found that the fuel had ignited on part of the engine’s exhaust system that had",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"发生案例\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:HAS_CASE {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_39 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:1a8d22464c3d1c3c",`source`:"shipkg:condition:7fb8a1a33328",`target`:"shipkg:fault:cdf116929c39",`properties`:{`name`:"触发",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:1a8d22464c3d1c3c",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:91f76498fecf4e21",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"43",`locator`:"PDF page 43",`quote`:"cating oil. In principle this was an entirely sensible precaution to protect the high voltage pod motor from damage. However, the low position of the bilge sensor meant that it could be activated by a relatively small amount of liquid that accumulated within the pod. Since the bilge suction probably did not extend low enough for the automatic bilge pumps to effectively pump the water out, it is likely the vessel’s motion in heavy weather caused the small amoun",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"触发\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:a224f41b8b7d6b98",`source`:"shipkg:fault:999defd690d8",`target`:"shipkg:symptom:674bee46af7f",`properties`:{`name`:"触发",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:a224f41b8b7d6b98",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:0e28dc346f51844d",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"ifold and catch fire. The small fire then ignited the engine high temperature alarm cabling loom, causing it to short circuit and set off the alarm in the wheelhouse (Figure 2). The functional fire and smoke alarm sensors were some distance from the fire, and the smoke and heat had not migrated that far by the time the master noticed the smoke on the camera monitor.",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"触发\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": true}"}},{`id`:"edge:a5a324438d9fb4aa",`source`:"shipkg:fault:e97eee073fc6",`target`:"shipkg:fault:c830e7992f26",`properties`:{`name`:"触发",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:true,`id`:"edge:a5a324438d9fb4aa",`case_id`:"spirit_of_discovery_pods_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:5d3cde311b090a6a",`source_file`:"MAIB_2026_06_Spirit_of_Discovery_propulsion_loss.pdf",`source_url`:"https://www.gov.uk/maib-reports/loss-of-propulsion-in-heavy-weather-experienced-by-the-passenger-vessel-spirit-of-discovery-leading-to-over-100-injuries-and-one-fatality",`page`:"42",`locator`:"PDF page 42",`quote`:"e rpm of each pod’s propulsion motor very rapidly increased and exceeded the preset overspeed limitation. The pod’s PCS therefore automatically tripped the power to its motor to prevent it being damaged. Spirit of Discovery’s engineers could likely have quickly reset the port and starboard motors and restored the vessel’s propulsion had the propulsion motor overspeed trips been the only issue. However",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"触发\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": true}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:TRIGGERS {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_40 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:1baaf26081652c9a",`source`:"shipkg:condition:a40db02fd2fa",`target`:"shipkg:action:6e0e5173ee8f",`properties`:{`name`:"削弱措施效果",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:1baaf26081652c9a",`case_id`:"sd2016_09_cpp_response",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:1ed28429bcfc3816",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"tion of this button bypassed the feedback control system, giving direct control of pitch to the pitch control lever. However, the master was not familiar with its use, and therefore lost the opportunity to bring the vessel back under control before it struck the quay. It was also revealed during the investigation that the system parameters for astern pitch control had been incorrectly set duri",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"削弱措施效果\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:23d24efd05e23e3e",`source`:"shipkg:condition:7a0e4d2405ef",`target`:"shipkg:action:9fa28e4c4571",`properties`:{`name`:"削弱措施效果",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:23d24efd05e23e3e",`case_id`:"windcat8_port_engine_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:e678a8a1bb3f1aec",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_01_Windcat8_bearing_failure_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/683922/MAIBInvReport01_2018.pdf",`page`:"11",`locator`:"PDF page 11",`quote`:"ire resulted from the ignition of oil vapour released from the damaged crankcase and did not spread beyond the port engine. • The fixed fire-fighting system was rendered ineffective because not all the port engine space vents were closed prior to its release. • The safety of the embarked technicians was given a high priority. ACTION TAKEN Windcat Workboats BV Ltd has: • Instructed crews on board vessels fitted with Volvo Penta D16 engines to stop the affected eng",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"削弱措施效果\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:REDUCES_EFFECTIVENESS_OF {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_41 }
CALL () { UNWIND [{`id`:"edge:1c38937cd6ac3b2a",`source`:"shipkg:condition:96f46a0b1ef9",`target`:"shipkg:condition:4277de3a84c9",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:1c38937cd6ac3b2a",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:412268fc761e9960",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"27",`locator`:"PDF page 27",`quote`:"ions. 2.4 HOT SPOT MONITORING Stena’s practice of measuring the temperature of running engines using an infrared spot thermometer had not identified the significant hazard posed by exposed surfaces of over 220°C that still existed post-accident after the insulation and shielding were replaced. The use of infrared spot thermometers in engine spaces limited their effectiveness as they could only prov",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:21c269f536ddda50",`source`:"shipkg:condition:db2e89c50479",`target`:"shipkg:fault:b2aa91be158b",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:21c269f536ddda50",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:3bea0430b472030b",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"64",`locator`:"PDF page 64",`quote`:"current imbalance transformer were tested during manufacture, subsequent tests of the system were by secondary current injection, bypassing the windings. As the IAS did not specifically register which rank of the HF had developed an imbalance current, it was not possible to confirm if the current imbalance transformers on rank 1 1.3 had ever worked in service. It is concerning th",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:45c48f589ff003ad",`source`:"shipkg:condition:290bfe38530e",`target`:"shipkg:fault:c44e6c4545bf",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:45c48f589ff003ad",`case_id`:"sd2016_05_cpp_backup",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:2d8d8f05ec0d8390",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"21",`locator`:"PDF page 21",`quote`:"tective covers over safety- critical buttons, switches and knobs. 2. The master was confident that he had control of his CPPs and did not look at the pitch indicators located on the control consoles. Had he done so he would have realised the starboard CPP was not responding to his orders. 3. The ship’s engineers recognised that something was untoward well before the master had committed to his",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:46fbc1fad6f5bc77",`source`:"shipkg:condition:19ae439543bd",`target`:"shipkg:fault:5f59e6b3ca42",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:46fbc1fad6f5bc77",`case_id`:"wight_sky_me_2017",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:9094aa614ec060db",`source_file`:"MAIB_2018_14_Wight_Sky_engine_bearing_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5b5217c7ed915d0b81e003df/MAIBInvReport14_2018.pdf",`page`:"14",`locator`:"PDF page 14",`quote`:"ntrolled environment and transferring it complete into the engine room would have reduced the likelihood of debris ingress. • The engine was not fitted with a wear detector, so there was no means of receiving a warning before the engine failed. • The essential services switchboard aft circuit breaker had been left in manual mode, resulting in the loss of power to critical equipment, including the fixed fire-fighting system. ACTION TAKEN Wightli",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:6ec0a6e6cf79dfff",`source`:"shipkg:condition:bdbca1b8295e",`target`:"shipkg:fault:439f73a406a0",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:6ec0a6e6cf79dfff",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:6522054ba5597880",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"16",`locator`:"PDF page 16",`quote`:"Although the indicator for the turning gear, which was sited on the control panel, showed that the turning gear was in, this was poorly illuminated and was not seen by the engineer. When the main engine start button was pressed to turn the engine on compressed air, a loud bang was heard; the turning gear interlock, the last remaining safety barrier, had failed to work. The resulting damage t",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:7fcc0c54724f2e91",`source`:"shipkg:condition:4a944c6dd633",`target`:"shipkg:condition:2d0261049d78",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:7fcc0c54724f2e91",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:d82fabc2bbd1fcf1",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"13",`locator`:"PDF page 13",`quote`:"e the aft HF from the electrical network. It was not possible to determine the exact cause of the subsequent blackout because the option for storing historical data concerning blackouts was not chosen at build. However, it is considered most likely that the disruption within the aft HF at the time of the accident caused general instability in the electrical network which could not be contained and led to the generators shuttin",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:978fd5dea39c2ab2",`source`:"shipkg:condition:4ae93bca9f29",`target`:"shipkg:fault:3349e319bedc",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:978fd5dea39c2ab2",`case_id`:"stena_europe_fuel_2023",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:9d1bc8efb3c65396",`source_file`:"MAIB_2024_20_Stena_Europe_fuel_spray_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6756db0ba63e1781efb87793/2024-20-StenaEurope.pdf",`page`:"27",`locator`:"PDF page 27",`quote`:"’s main engine fuel systems were historically reported in the vessel’s DOCMAP system. However, this had stopped over time and the crew instead repaired the leaks and recorded them locally in the engine room logbook. The relatively high turnover and heavy workload of engine room crew had resulted in defect reporting being considered a low priority, which had led to the requirements in SMS document SMM-0255 not bein",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:ab901de38913b7d7",`source`:"shipkg:condition:133adfa97595",`target`:"shipkg:consequence:81fff36694d8",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:ab901de38913b7d7",`case_id`:"sd2016_22_cooling_pipe",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:6a6ede2b06a7fa26",`source_file`:"MAIB_2016_Safety_Digest_generator_oil_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e81e5d2d3bf7f13416961fa/2016-SD1-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"60",`locator`:"PDF page 60",`quote`:"are supper. Although the bilge alarm operated as designed, with no one present in the wheelhouse to either see or hear it, it was not detected in time to save the vessel. Never leave the wheelhouse unmanned when underway; doing so is in contravention of the COLREGs and puts you and your vessel at risk. 2. The crew were instructed to enter the accommodation to collect lifejackets in preparation fo",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:bd71a40255f6239a",`source`:"shipkg:condition:94ebbaf1c3c4",`target`:"shipkg:consequence:775549e4c085",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:bd71a40255f6239a",`case_id`:"sd2013_12_oily_rag",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:db9d3c4ba46b3f43",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"41",`locator`:"PDF page 41",`quote`:"off the alarm in the wheelhouse (Figure 2). The functional fire and smoke alarm sensors were some distance from the fire, and the smoke and heat had not migrated that far by the time the master noticed the smoke on the camera monitor.",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:e4dc29615b38ae3d",`source`:"shipkg:condition:4fe499c68172",`target`:"shipkg:fault:1e5a23a200ad",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:e4dc29615b38ae3d",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:a761595279b52f7c",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"29",`locator`:"PDF page 29",`quote`:"ey need to be checked to ensure they continue to function correctly. However, in the case of Pride of Canterbury these valves had never been tested or inspected since the ship was constructed 23 years previously. The LIPS CPP system manual provided some maintenance instructions, including annual testing of pressure safety valve (PSV1) and the back pressure valve (PSV3). However, how this",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:e6a307f3b94eadaf",`source`:"shipkg:condition:7d61f4e32250",`target`:"shipkg:fault:8027eb707475",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:e6a307f3b94eadaf",`case_id`:"sd2013_03_turning_gear",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:4ed3569c8bb32f4f",`source_file`:"MAIB_2013_Safety_Digest_lubrication_bearing_cases.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/876748/2013-SD2-MAIBSafetyDigest.pdf",`page`:"18",`locator`:"PDF page 18",`quote`:"CASE 3 17MAIB Safety Digest 2/2013 The Lessons 1. The turning gear interlock had not been included within the planned maintenance system on board and there was no record of it having been tested. 2. Control console illumination panels are vital to the safe operation of machinery and should therefore be tested regularly. If problems with visual indication or warnin",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:eb00e74b105c9e6b",`source`:"shipkg:condition:4dcab8c954bb",`target`:"shipkg:fault:1e5a23a200ad",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:eb00e74b105c9e6b",`case_id`:"pride_can_cpp_2014",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:7058770c39736963",`source_file`:"MAIB_2015_22_Pride_of_Canterbury_CPP_hydraulic_fire.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/563092daed915d566d000002/MAIBInvReport-22_2015.pdf",`page`:"30",`locator`:"PDF page 30",`quote`:"24 the valves and their refitting was deemed an unnecessary measure. However, the oil sampling programme had not identified the wear in the back pressure valve as it had, most likely, occurred gradually over a long period of time. 2.3.3 Pipework joints and shielding Whereas the main components of Pride of Canterbury’s CPP system were supplied after testing by",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}},{`id`:"edge:f08fa036f145759a",`source`:"shipkg:fault:b2aa91be158b",`target`:"shipkg:fault:5737f3610967",`properties`:{`name`:"妨碍发现",`graph_version`:"4.1",`is_causal`:false,`id`:"edge:f08fa036f145759a",`case_id`:"queen_mary2_hf_2010",`certainty`:"reported",`certainty_zh`:"报告明确记载",`evidence_id`:"ev:ab39293c5f3260fc",`source_file`:"MAIB_2011_28_Queen_Mary_2_harmonic_filter_failure.pdf",`source_url`:"https://assets.digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk/media/547c6fa6ed915d4c10000031/QM2Report.pdf",`page`:"64",`locator`:"PDF page 64",`quote`:"ious problems. 2.4.5 Current imbalance detection system The capacitor exploded because the inoperative imbalance detection system could not identify the deterioration of the capacitors. The failure of the imbalance system’s current transformer remained undetected for what could have been several years. It is certain that this system was not working in 2008 when Converteam detected two defective capacitors durin",`props_json`:"{\"name\": \"妨碍发现\", \"graph_version\": \"4.1\", \"is_causal\": false}"}}] AS row MATCH (a:ShipKG {id:row.source}), (b:ShipKG {id:row.target}) MERGE (a)-[r:LIMITS_DETECTION_OF {id:row.id}]->(b) SET r += row.properties RETURN count(r) AS processed_42 }
